COLLDATA("tadabburen","en",[[460,"§Az-Zumar\ndeeds\nCollaborate with a family member on a good deed in the hope that you all will win on the Day of Resurrection.\nListen to verses from the Book of Allah and implement them.\nListen to a lecture or a sermon at a mosque and implement what is said.\nguid\nSincerity in religion and worship is one of the qualities of the Holy Prophet (ﷺ).\nA sound person remembers the awful punishment before committing a sin.\nThe biggest losers among people are those who will lose themselves and their families on the Day of Resurrection.\nrefl\nقُلۡ إِنِّيٓ أُمِرۡتُ أَنۡ أَعۡبُدَ ٱللَّهَ مُخۡلِصٗا لَّهُ ٱلدِّينَ ١١ وَأُمِرۡتُ لِأَنۡ أَكُونَ أَوَّلَ ٱلۡمُسۡلِمِينَ ١٢\nSomeone may ask: Why is the phrase, (I have been commanded) repeated while it indicates similar meanings in both places? The answer is: The first command is to worship with sincerity, while the second command is to hasten to Islam. Hence, they convey two different meanings. Ibn Juzay: 2/266.\nThe phrase, (I have been commanded) is repeated to exhort two things. What are they?\nوَأُمِرۡتُ لِأَنۡ أَكُونَ أَوَّلَ ٱلۡمُسۡلِمِينَ ١٢\nBecause I am the one who calls and guides people to their Lord, which dictates that I should be the first one to comply with what I enjoin, and the first one to submit to Allah in Islam. This should be the case on the part of Muhammad (ﷺ) and on the part of those who claim to be his followers. Al-Saadi: 721.\nThe Holy Quran exhorts Muslims to hold fast to the religion. Explain in light of this verse.\nقُلۡ إِنَّ ٱلۡخَٰسِرِينَ ٱلَّذِينَ خَسِرُوٓاْ أَنفُسَهُمۡ وَأَهۡلِيهِمۡ يَوۡمَ ٱلۡقِيَٰمَةِۗ\nMeaning: They will be separated and will never meet again, whether their families have gone to Paradise while they have gone to Hell, or all of them have gone to Hell, they will never meet or feel happiness again. Ibn Kathir: 4/49.\nIf the disobedient people enter the Fire on the Day of Resurrection with their families, will they be happy with them?\nٱلَّذِينَ يَسۡتَمِعُونَ ٱلۡقَوۡلَ فَيَتَّبِعُونَ أَحۡسَنَهُۥٓۚ\nIbn Abbas said: \"This refers to one who listens to the good speech and the bad one, but speaks the good and turns away from the bad.\" Moreover, it is said: “They listen to the Quran and other things, and follow the Quran.\" Al-Qurtubi: 18/260.\nlistening to speech and following the best of it. How?\nٱلَّذِينَ يَسۡتَمِعُونَ ٱلۡقَوۡلَ فَيَتَّبِعُونَ أَحۡسَنَهُۥٓۚ أُوْلَٰٓئِكَ ٱلَّذِينَ هَدَىٰهُمُ ٱللَّهُۖ وَأُوْلَٰٓئِكَ هُمۡ أُوْلُواْ ٱلۡأَلۡبَٰبِ ١٨\nThis refers to all that is said. They listen to all types of speech that they hear, in order to distinguish between what should be given precedence and what should be avoided. It is a sign of their prudence and maturity in thinking that they follow the best of speech. The best of all speech is the words of Allah and the words of His Messenger (r), as Allah mentions later in this Surah: (Allah has sent down the best message – a consistent Book of repeated lessons) [39:23]. The one who does not distinguish between good words and bad words is not one of those of sound reasoning. As for the one who distinguishes between them, but his whims and desires overwhelm his rational thinking, and his rational thinking becomes captive to his whims and desires, so, he does not give precedence to what is best, then he is a man of no understanding. Al-Saadi: 722.\nHow would you judge someone as having sound reasoning?\nٱلَّذِينَ يَسۡتَمِعُونَ ٱلۡقَوۡلَ فَيَتَّبِعُونَ أَحۡسَنَهُۥٓۚ أُوْلَٰٓئِكَ ٱلَّذِينَ هَدَىٰهُمُ ٱللَّهُۖ وَأُوْلَٰٓئِكَ هُمۡ أُوْلُواْ ٱلۡأَلۡبَٰبِ ١٨\nThey listen to the Quran, and follow its best through their deeds, like choosing to forgive rather than retaliate, and akin to that. Ibn Juzay: 2/267.\nIn light of the interpretation of this verse, how can someone follow the best of speech?\nأَفَمَنۡ حَقَّ عَلَيۡهِ كَلِمَةُ ٱلۡعَذَابِ أَفَأَنتَ تُنقِذُ مَن فِي ٱلنَّارِ ١٩\nHere, the verb (save) brings a comparison of the attitude of the Prophet (ﷺ) toward the disbelievers, where he was keen to guide them while they were immersed in what would lead them to the Fire, to someone who tries to save another who is in the middle of the Fire and surrounded by it. Ibn Ashur: 23/371.\nGiven this verse, show the Prophet's (ﷺ) strive to guide all the people.\nwords\nظُلَلٌ مِنَ النَّارِLayers of fire similar to canopies\nالطَّاغُوتَsatan or any false objects of worship\nوَأَنَابُواThey turned back to Allah in repentance and obedience\nفَسَلَكَهُ يَنَابِيعَHe makes it flow as springs and rivers\nيَهِيجُIt becomes dry\nحُطَامًاCrumbled and debris"],[461,"§Az-Zumar\ndeeds\nSay the morning and evening Athkar (remembrance of Allah), as it reassures the heart.\nRead a book on the causes of humbleness when reciting the Quran.\nDo your utmost today to reflect on the meanings of the Holy Quran.\nguid\nKnow that true guidance is in the hand of Allah, and not anyone else, so, ask Him for it at all times.\nWhoever does not refrain from disobeying Allah in worldly life, his face will not shield him from the worst of the punishment on the Day of Resurrection.\nBe certain that all people will die, therefore, be ready when your time comes.\nrefl\nأَفَمَن شَرَحَ ٱللَّهُ صَدۡرَهُۥ لِلۡإِسۡلَٰمِ فَهُوَ عَلَىٰ نُورٖ مِّن رَّبِّهِۦۚ\nChoosing the word, (Opened) to indicate acceptance of Islam, because Islam's teachings, morals, and etiquettes earn the Muslim joy with himself, happiness for his Lord’s pleasure with him, and belittlement of hardships facing him, knowing for certain that he is on his side of truth, will be rewarded for his affliction, hoping for his Lord's mercy in this world and the Hereafter, and no doubts or bewilderment cross his mind. Ibn Ashur: 23/380\nExplain the relevancy of using the word, (Opened) to indicate acceptance of Islam.\nفَوَيۡلٞ لِّلۡقَٰسِيَةِ قُلُوبُهُم مِّن ذِكۡرِ ٱللَّهِۚ أُوْلَٰٓئِكَ فِي ضَلَٰلٖ مُّبِينٍ ٢٢\nMalik bin Dinar said: \"No servant is punished more severely than one whose heart is hardened, and whenever Allah becomes angry with some people, He removes mercy from them.\" Al-Baghawi: 4/12\nWhat is the most severe punishment suffered by a servant?\nيَٰٓأَيُّهَا ٱلنَّبِيُّ جَٰهِدِ ٱلۡكُفَّارَ وَٱلۡمُنَٰفِقِينَ\nBeing harsh with them is a part of being submissive to Allah while being lenient with the people of Allah is a part of fearing Him. In the beginning, Allah commanded His Messenger to be lenient with them to leave them no excuse, and reveal their stubbornness; however, when leniency was exhausted, He commanded Him to be harsh with them. Al-Biqai: 20/206.\nWhen is it required for one to be harsh with disbelievers and the hypocrites?\nٱللَّهُ نَزَّلَ أَحۡسَنَ ٱلۡحَدِيثِ\nThe Quran is the best message because it contains the best narration of useful meanings, which comprise the essence of faith, Sharia, inference, emphasis on the greatness of the worlds, the creatures, and the wonders of the making of man and his mind. Moreover, it propagates good manners, and calls on the minds to reflect and infer the truth with its articulate wordings and eloquent meanings that are inimitable. Ibn Ashur: 23/385.\nThe Quran is the best message. Why?\nٱللَّهُ نَزَّلَ أَحۡسَنَ ٱلۡحَدِيثِ كِتَٰبٗا مُّتَشَٰبِهٗا مَّثَانِيَ\nMeaning: Its stories and rulings, and the descriptions of good people and evil people, are repeated, and the names and attributes of Allah are repeated. These meanings and ideas are, for people’s hearts, like water for trees; the less frequently trees are watered, the more they are damaged and they may even be destroyed, but the more frequently they are watered, the better they are and the more beneficial fruit they may bear. In like manner, the heart constantly needs to be reminded of the meanings and ideas in the word of Allah. Similarly, the reader of the Quran should reflect on its meanings and should not omit to reflect on the meanings of all verses, because that is a means of attaining much good and many benefits. Al-Saadi: 723.\nWhat is the wisdom behind the repeated meanings in different places in the Quran?\nتَقۡشَعِرُّ مِنۡهُ جُلُودُ ٱلَّذِينَ يَخۡشَوۡنَ رَبَّهُمۡ ثُمَّ تَلِينُ جُلُودُهُمۡ وَقُلُوبُهُمۡ إِلَىٰ ذِكۡرِ ٱللَّهِۚ ذَٰلِكَ هُدَى ٱللَّهِ يَهۡدِي بِهِۦ مَن يَشَآءُۚ وَمَن يُضۡلِلِ ٱللَّهُ فَمَا لَهُۥ مِنۡ هَادٍ ٢٣\nIf one says: Why are the skins mentioned alone first, then they are mentioned with the hearts? The answer is: When Allah says, (shiver), He mentions the skins alone since shivering is the sole attribute of the skins. Then, when He says, (soften), He mentions the skins and hearts since softening is an attribute of both, the skins and hearts. It shivers first from fear, then it softens with hope. Ibn Juzay: 2/268.\nWhy are the skins mentioned alone first, then they are mentioned with the hearts?\nوَضَرَبَ ٱللَّهُ مَثَلٗا لِّلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُواْ ٱمۡرَأَتَ فِرۡعَوۡنَ إِذۡ قَالَتۡ رَبِّ ٱبۡنِ لِي عِندَكَ بَيۡتٗا فِي ٱلۡجَنَّةِ وَنَجِّنِي مِن فِرۡعَوۡنَ وَعَمَلِهِۦ وَنَجِّنِي مِنَ ٱلۡقَوۡمِ ٱلظَّٰلِمِينَ ١١\nThe point of this example is that the relationship of a believer with a disbeliever does not harm the believer if he parted with him in his disbelief and deeds. The sins of others will not harm the obedient believer in the Hereafter. The believer may be subject to a general punishment that befalls the people of the earth when they neglect the commands of Allah. The wife of Pharaoh was never harmed by her ties to Pharaoh, who was the worst of all disbelievers. Ibn Al-Qayim: 3/170.\nWhat must the believer do when he finds himself in a relationship with a disbeliever?\nأَفَمَن يَتَّقِي بِوَجۡهِهِۦ سُوٓءَ ٱلۡعَذَابِ يَوۡمَ ٱلۡقِيَٰمَةِۚ\nOn that day, he will be faced with immense punishment and he will try to shield himself with his face, which is the noblest part of the body, and the least of punishment may have an impact on it. He will try to shield himself with it from the terrible punishment because his hands and feet will be tied up. Al-Saadi: 723.\nThe dwellers of the Fire will try to shield with their faces the punishment. Why?\nوَلَقَدۡ ضَرَبۡنَا لِلنَّاسِ فِي هَٰذَا ٱلۡقُرۡءَانِ مِن كُلِّ مَثَلٖ لَّعَلَّهُمۡ يَتَذَكَّرُونَ ٢٧\nAmong the features of the Quran, the examples are singled out for mention in order to attract their attention to reflect on a great aspect of its inimitability, which are its eloquent examples, for their eloquent people used to compete in the excellence of examples. Ibn Ashur: 23/397.\nThe examples in the Quran are singled out for mention. Why?\nwords\nمَثَانِيَIts rulings, narrations and proof are repeated\nتَقشَعِرُّShivers\nتَلِينُSoftens\nعِوَجٍDeviation\nمُتَشَاكِسُونَQuarreling partners"],[462,"§Az-Zumar\ndeeds\nStarting today, ensure that you say the truth during your serious and humorous times.\nSay, \"O Changer of the hearts, make my heart firm upon Your religion.\"\nSay this supplication, \"Allah suffices me, there is none worthy of worship but Him. I have placed my trust in Him, He is the Lord of the Majestic Throne.\"\nguid\nTruthfulness is of great importance to attain piety toward Allah, hence, be truthful with yourself and others.\nWhen you truly submit to Allah, He will suffice and protect you.\nConcern yourself with fearing Allah, no matter how many threatening people you face.\nrefl\n۞فَمَنۡ أَظۡلَمُ مِمَّن كَذَبَ عَلَى ٱللَّهِ وَكَذَّبَ بِٱلصِّدۡقِ إِذۡ جَآءَهُۥٓۚ أَلَيۡسَ فِي جَهَنَّمَ مَثۡوٗى لِّلۡكَٰفِرِينَ ٣٢\nThey had committed many acts of grave wrongdoings; violating the sanctity of the Lord by lying about His attributes, lying against Him by claiming that He commanded them to practice their falsehood, denying the Messenger, attributing falsehood to the Quran, causing annoyance to the believers, flipping the facts about the world and corrupting them, and causing the infliction of eternal punishment on themselves. Ibn Ashur: 24/5.\nList some of the wrongdoings for which the polytheists deserved to be described as, the most unjust among people.\nوَٱلَّذِي جَآءَ بِٱلصِّدۡقِ وَصَدَّقَ بِهِۦٓ أُوْلَٰٓئِكَ هُمُ ٱلۡمُتَّقُونَ ٣٣\nAll characteristics of piety and righteousness boil down to proclaiming the truth and believing in it. Al-Saadi: 724.\nWhat is the link between righteousness and saying the truth and believing in it?\nأَلَيۡسَ ٱللَّهُ بِكَافٍ عَبۡدَهُۥۖ وَيُخَوِّفُونَكَ بِٱلَّذِينَ مِن دُونِهِۦۚ\nAllah honors the Messenger (ﷺ) greatly by attributing his servitude to Him, (His servant), which also, indicates that Allah will never abandon him to his enemies. Ibn Ashur: 24/13.\nExplain how the Prophet (ﷺ) is honored by Allah in light of this verse.\nأَلَيۡسَ ٱللَّهُ بِكَافٍ عَبۡدَهُۥۖ وَيُخَوِّفُونَكَ بِٱلَّذِينَ مِن دُونِهِۦۚ\n(Is not Allah sufficient for His servant), this strengthens the soul of the Prophet (ﷺ), because the disbelievers of Quraish threatened him with their idols and said: O Muhammad, you revile them, and we are afraid that they may inflict you with madness or other sickness. So, this verse was revealed in response to them. Ibn Atiyah: 4/532.\nWhat should be the position of the believer if he is threatened with created beings? Explain in light of this verse.\nأَلَيۡسَ ٱللَّهُ بِعَزِيزٖ ذِي ٱنتِقَامٖ ٣٧\nIf the polytheists profess to Allah's above-mentioned attributes, then they would have to know that Allah, the All-Mighty, would suffice His servant. So, no one could inflict harm on him, and that He would take retribution from those who intended harm to His servant. Ibn Ashur: 24/15.\nThis verse ends with these two attributes, (All-Mighty, Capable of Retribution). Why?\nقُلۡ يَٰقَوۡمِ ٱعۡمَلُواْ عَلَىٰ مَكَانَتِكُمۡ إِنِّي عَٰمِلٞۖ فَسَوۡفَ تَعۡلَمُونَ ٣٩ مَن يَأۡتِيهِ عَذَابٞ يُخۡزِيهِ وَيَحِلُّ عَلَيۡهِ عَذَابٞ مُّقِيمٌ ٤٠\nAfter Allah has fully admonished and presented the clearest proof to them, and kept firm His Messenger (ﷺ), He commanded His Messenger (ﷺ) to stand aside in anticipation of near victory, and promise them an awaited loss. Ibn Ashur: 24/1.\nHow does this verse pertain to the verses before it?\nمَن يَأۡتِيهِ عَذَابٞ يُخۡزِيهِ وَيَحِلُّ عَلَيۡهِ عَذَابٞ مُّقِيمٌ ٤٠\n(A humiliating punishment), a punishment by killing them, taking them captives, subjecting them to hunger and drought; and all of that happened to the polytheists in Makkah and in the battle of Badr. (And upon whom will descend an everlasting punishment), which is the Fire punishment in the Hereafter. We seek refuge with Allah from both punishments; the humiliating punishment in worldly life and the Fire punishment in the Hereafter. Al-Jaza'iri: 4/490.\nWhat is the difference between the humiliating punishment and the everlasting punishment?\nwords\nبِالصِّدقِWith the truth\nمَثوىًA residence\nحَسبِيَSufficient for me\nمَكَانَتِكُمYour position\nيُخزِيهِHumiliates him"],[463,"§Az-Zumar\ndeeds\nWhenever you go to sleep, say, \"O Allah, I submitted my soul to You, I have turned my face toward You, I entrusted my affair to You, and committed my back to You in hope and fear of You. There is no refuge or safe haven from You except with You. I believed in Your Book which You have revealed and in Your Prophet whom You have sent.\"\nRemember Allah, the Almighty, with a variety of Athkar.\nIdentify a deed that you are skeptical about its authenticity, and ask a scholar about its ruling.\nguid\nOne of the righteous predecessors said: An hour of reflection is better than praying all night without reflection.\nIntercession is all in the hands of Allah, so, seek it from Him.\nEnsure to monitor your deeds for sincere intention and conformity to the Sunnah.\nrefl\nٱللَّهُ يَتَوَفَّى ٱلۡأَنفُسَ حِينَ مَوۡتِهَا\nThe fact that Allah attributes this action to Himself does not contradict the fact that He has appointed the Angel of Death and his helpers to do this task, because He may attribute things to Himself in the sense that He is the Creator and controller thereof, or He may attribute them to their causes, in the sense that it is His way and wisdom to make a cause for everything. Al-Saadi: 725.\nHow do we reconcile the taking of the souls at the time of death by Allah and by the Angel of death?\nإِنَّ فِي ذَٰلِكَ لَأٓيَٰتٖ لِّقَوۡمٖ يَتَفَكَّرُونَ ٤٢\nMeaning: Signs of His capability, where He does not mistake the souls that should be held and the ones that should be sent. Muqatil said: Signs for those who reflect on the matter of resurrection, which means that taking the soul of a sleeping person, then, resending it back to him is proof of resurrection. Al-Baghawi: 4/19.\nExplain how withholding the souls and resending them during sleep is proof of the resurrection.\nأَمِ ٱتَّخَذُواْ مِن دُونِ ٱللَّهِ شُفَعَآءَۚ قُلۡ أَوَلَوۡ كَانُواْ لَا يَمۡلِكُونَ شَيۡـٔٗا وَلَا يَعۡقِلُونَ ٤٣\nSince intercession is something intangible, then, its possession means attaining its result. This verse ridicules their claim that these inanimate objects would intercede for them; how would they intercede when they do not reason? The absence of their minds negates any thought about intercession, let alone having the will to do it. Indeed, considering them as intercessors is foolishness. Ibn Ashur: 24/27.\nHow are the polytheists ridiculed for considering their idols as intercessors?\nقُل لِّلَّهِ ٱلشَّفَٰعَةُ جَمِيعٗاۖ لَّهُۥ مُلۡكُ ٱلسَّمَٰوَٰتِ وَٱلۡأَرۡضِۖ\nThis is an affirmation that intercession belongs to Allah alone. As He said, (Who is there that can intercede with Him except with His permission) [2:255]. Al-Qurtubi: 18/289\nDoes anyone else besides Allah possess intercession?\nوَإِذَا ذُكِرَ ٱللَّهُ وَحۡدَهُ ٱشۡمَأَزَّتۡ قُلُوبُ ٱلَّذِينَ لَا يُؤۡمِنُونَ بِٱلۡأٓخِرَةِۖ\nMeaning: The disbelievers detest the Oneness of Allah, and like to associate partners with Him. (Shrink with aversion), their hearts become constricted due to their hatred for that. Ibn Juzay: 2/271\nHow do you infer from this verse that the Oneness of Allah is inclusive of heart's deeds?\nقُلِ ٱللَّهُمَّ فَاطِرَ ٱلسَّمَٰوَٰتِ وَٱلۡأَرۡضِ عَٰلِمَ ٱلۡغَيۡبِ وَٱلشَّهَٰدَةِ أَنتَ تَحۡكُمُ بَيۡنَ عِبَادِكَ فِي مَا كَانُواْ فِيهِ يَخۡتَلِفُونَ ٤٦\nThis description, (Creator of the heavens and the earth) highlights the attribute of Allah’s Power that is mentioned before His Knowledge attribute, because people realize His power before realizing His knowledge. Moreover, the power is relevant to judging between His servants, since judgment entails compulsion and subjugation which are the direct results of power. Ibn Ashur: 24/31.\nHow does this verse pertain to the verses before it?\nوَبَدَا لَهُم مِّنَ ٱللَّهِ مَا لَمۡ يَكُونُواْ يَحۡتَسِبُونَ ٤٧\nMujahid said: They performed deeds that they thought were righteous, but they will turn out to be evil. Or, it is possible that they thought they would be forgiven without repentance. (And there will appear to them from Allah what they had never anticipated) of entering the Fire. On this verse, Sufyan Al-Thawri said: Woe to the pretentious ones, woe to the pretentious ones; that is their verse and their story. Ikrimah bin Ammar said: Muhammad bin Munkadir grieved intensely at the time of his death, then he was asked: What was this grief about? He replied: I am frightened of one verse in the Book of Allah, (And there will appear to them from Allah what they had never anticipated), I am frightened that there will appear to me what I had never anticipated. Al-Qurtubi: 18/289.\nWill it be possible to find evil in the place of what you thought was good on the Day of Resurrection?\nwords\nيَتَوَفَّىTakes away the souls\nاشْمَأَزَّتShrink with aversion\nفَاطِرَThe Creator\nالغَيْبِ والشَّهَادَةِThe unseen and the witnessed\nيَحْتَسِبُونَAnticipate, expect"],[464,"§Az-Zumar\ndeeds\nList three of Allah's greatest blessings on you, then thank Him for them.\nSay, \"O Allah, forgive all of my sins: the small and great, the first and last, the open and secret.\"\nAsk Allah to make His blessings upon you a reason for your modesty and closeness to Him, and seek refuge with your Lord from their temptations.\nguid\nBeware of Allah's trial of you with blessings, for how many blessed persons who are being tested and allured gradually to punishment while they do not know .\nBe content with Allah in all His decrees, for He extends and restricts provision for whomever He wills.\nIf glad tidings of forgiveness and mercy are given to those who transgressed against themselves, then it will be even more so for others. So, hasten for repentance.\nrefl\nوَبَدَا لَهُمۡ سَيِّـَٔاتُ مَا كَسَبُواْ وَحَاقَ بِهِم مَّا كَانُواْ بِهِۦ يَسۡتَهۡزِءُونَ ٤٨\nThe verb (earned) is used here and not \"did\", in order to put an end to their discontent with the punishment by confirming that they themselves had earned its causes, similar to this verse, (And it will be said to the wrongdoers, \"Taste what you used to earn\") [39:24], instead of \"do.\" Ibn Ashur: 24/34.\nThe verb (earned) is used here and not \"did\", why?\nفَإِذَا مَسَّ ٱلۡإِنسَٰنَ ضُرّٞ دَعَانَا\nThis verse reveals the fact that the disbelievers of Quraish used to believe in the Lordship of Allah. Hence, they were better than the Bolshevik communists who did not believe in Allah. Moreover, the disbelievers of Quraish were better than some ignorant Muslims of today, since when they faced adversity, they called upon Allah with devoted sincerity to Him Alone, but the ignorant Muslims of today associate partners to Him during prosperity and adversity by invoking the righteous and the dead, and seeking their help at all times. Al-Jaza'iri: 4/498.\nThe disbelievers of Quraish were better than some ignorant Muslims of today. Why?\nقَالَ إِنَّمَآ أُوتِيتُهُۥ عَلَىٰ عِلۡمِۢ\nThis may be interpreted in two ways; first (the most probable) is that he means his know-how of earning and benefitting. Second: Allah knows that I deserve this. Ibn Juzay: 2/271.\nThis verse points out to the delusion of wealth’s owner by himself. Explain.\nثُمَّ إِذَا خَوَّلۡنَٰهُ نِعۡمَةٗ مِّنَّا قَالَ إِنَّمَآ أُوتِيتُهُۥ عَلَىٰ عِلۡمِۢ بَلۡ هِيَ فِتۡنَةٞ وَلَٰكِنَّ أَكۡثَرَهُمۡ لَا يَعۡلَمُونَ ٤٩\n(Because of knowledge), Allah knows that I deserve it. Muqatil said: Allah knows that I am good. (Rather, it is a trial), this blessing is an alluring trial, a test, and an affliction. Al-Baghawi: 4/21.\nIs every blessing considered to be good for man? Explain in light of this verse.\nبَلۡ هِيَ فِتۡنَةٞ وَلَٰكِنَّ أَكۡثَرَهُمۡ لَا يَعۡلَمُونَ ٤٩\n(But most of them do not know), and therefore they regard the test as a blessing, and they are confused between something that is definitely good and something that may be a cause of good or a source of trouble. Al-Saadi: 727.\nA blessing may be risky for a heedless ignorant person. Why?\nأَوَ لَمۡ يَعۡلَمُوٓاْ أَنَّ ٱللَّهَ يَبۡسُطُ ٱلرِّزۡقَ لِمَن يَشَآءُ وَيَقۡدِرُۚ إِنَّ فِي ذَٰلِكَ لَأٓيَٰتٖ لِّقَوۡمٖ يُؤۡمِنُونَ ٥٢\nMeaning: In the bestowing or withholding of provision, because those who believe know that this matter is connected to divine wisdom and mercy, and that Allah knows best the condition of His servants. He may restrict provision to them out of kindness toward them, because if He grants them abundant provision, they will go beyond the bounds and spread injustice in the land. Hence, by doing that, He is taking care of their spiritual interests, which are the essence of their happiness and prosperity. Al-Saadi: 727.\nA little provision is a sign of Allah's kindness and mercy to His servants. How?\n۞قُلۡ يَٰعِبَادِيَ ٱلَّذِينَ أَسۡرَفُواْ عَلَىٰٓ أَنفُسِهِمۡ لَا تَقۡنَطُواْ مِن رَّحۡمَةِ ٱللَّهِۚ إِنَّ ٱللَّهَ يَغۡفِرُ ٱلذُّنُوبَ جَمِيعًاۚ إِنَّهُۥ هُوَ ٱلۡغَفُورُ ٱلرَّحِيمُ ٥٣\nThe previous verses expand on warning that induces fear in the hearts of the listeners, despite their show of disregard. However, this could lead them to despair, hence, Allah sends a message of hope afterward in order to bring them out to the safety of the land if they want to. This promise and warning adheres to the style of this Glorious Book in treating the souls. Ibn Ashur: 24/39.\nHow does this verse pertain to the verses before it?\nwords\nوَحَاقَSurrounded them from all sides\nخَوَّلنَاهُWe bestow on him\nوَأَنِيبُواReturn in repentance\nفَرَّطتُI neglected\nجَنبِ اللهِObedience and duty to Allah"],[465,"§Az-Zumar\ndeeds\nPraise Allah and thank Him for all His blessings, the greatest of which is the blessing of being Muslim.\nGratitude to Allah is a reason for ridding self-admiration due to righteous deeds. Thank Allah often today for helping you to do righteous deeds.\nWrite a short message in which you explain the manifestations of Allah's greatness.\nguid\nBeware of arrogance, as arrogant people will be afflicted with disgrace on the Day of Resurrection.\nUphold the fear of Allah, for it is the way to salvation.\nIgnorance is a reason for shirk, so work on learning the knowledge of Sharia as much as possible.\nrefl\nأَوۡ تَقُولَ لَوۡ أَنَّ ٱللَّهَ هَدَىٰنِي لَكُنتُ مِنَ ٱلۡمُتَّقِينَ ٥٧ أَوۡ تَقُولَ حِينَ تَرَى ٱلۡعَذَابَ لَوۡ أَنَّ لِي كَرَّةٗ فَأَكُونَ مِنَ ٱلۡمُحۡسِنِينَ ٥٨\nTheir thoughts are stated in the natural sequence as they come to their minds. Starting with regret for what they had brought about on themselves, then, apology and disavowal of their actions hoping it will save them, then, wishing to go back to worldly life to do good, as Allah says, (he says, \"My Lord, send me back ` so that I may do righteous deeds in what I left behind\"). Thus, this order of describing the events is very precise. Ibn Ashur: 24/47.\nThe verses describe the soul’s sequence of thoughts in an orderly manner. Explain\nوَيَوۡمَ ٱلۡقِيَٰمَةِ تَرَى ٱلَّذِينَ كَذَبُواْ عَلَى ٱللَّهِ وُجُوهُهُم مُّسۡوَدَّةٌۚ أَلَيۡسَ فِي جَهَنَّمَ مَثۡوٗى لِّلۡمُتَكَبِّرِينَ ٦٠\nDescribing them as (arrogant) indicates that punishing them by blackening their faces is appropriate for their arrogance, because when an arrogant person has a bad face, his arrogance will diminish, for arrogance will abate commensurate with the person's awareness of people's knowledge of his shortcomings. Ibn Ashur: 24/5.\nWhat is the wisdom behind punishing the arrogant by blackening their faces?\nوَيُنَجِّي ٱللَّهُ ٱلَّذِينَ ٱتَّقَوۡاْ بِمَفَازَتِهِمۡ لَا يَمَسُّهُمُ ٱلسُّوٓءُ وَلَا هُمۡ يَحۡزَنُونَ ٦١\n(And Allah will save those who feared Him) from Hellfire because they are not arrogant. This indicates that fearing Allah contradicts arrogance, as fearing Allah is the ultimate quality in Sharia, which entails avoiding all evils and adhering to Allah's command outwardly and inwardly; and arrogance is an inward heart sickness. Ibn Ashur: 24/52.\nWhat is the use of mentioning those who fear Allah after mentioning the arrogant?\nٱللَّهُ خَٰلِقُ كُلِّ شَيۡءٖۖ\nThis and similar phrases, which appear frequently in the Quran, indicate that all things - apart from Allah and His names and attributes - are created. This is a refutation of all those who say that some created things exist since eternity, such as the philosophers who say that the earth and the heavens exist since eternity, or those who say that souls exist since eternity, and other views that are based on falsehood and implicitly deny the Creator. Al-Saadi: 728.\nHow do you respond to those who say that some created things exist since eternity? What are the implications of such claim?\nقُلۡ أَفَغَيۡرَ ٱللَّهِ تَأۡمُرُوٓنِّيٓ أَعۡبُدُ أَيُّهَا ٱلۡجَٰهِلُونَ ٦٤\nMeaning: This stems from your ignorance, otherwise if you knew that Allah, Who is perfect in all aspects, the Bestower of all blessings, is the only One Who is deserving of worship, and not those who are lacking in all aspects and cannot bring benefit or cause harm, you would not order me to do that. Al-Saadi: 729.\nThe polytheists are described as the (ignorant ones). Why?\nبَلِ ٱللَّهَ فَٱعۡبُدۡ وَكُن مِّنَ ٱلشَّٰكِرِينَ ٦٦\n(And be among those who are grateful) for His guidance. Just as Allah is to be thanked for worldly blessings, such as physical good health and well-being, granting provision, and so on, He is also to be thanked and praised for spiritual blessings, such as enabling one to be sincere and to fear Him. In fact, it is spiritual blessings that are the real blessings. Al-Saadi: 729.\nThe verse ends with (and be among those who are grateful). Why?\nبَلِ ٱللَّهَ فَٱعۡبُدۡ وَكُن مِّنَ ٱلشَّٰكِرِينَ ٦٦\nPondering and realizing that they come from Allah and giving thanks to Him for them will protect the person from self-admiration that affects many people who strive hard, because of their ignorance. Otherwise, if a person were to understand the reality of things, he would not develop self-admiration because of the blessing which requires him to give more thanks to Allah. Al-Saadi: 729.\nThis verse guides to ridding of the delusion and self-admiration that may happen to those who do righteous deeds. Explain.\nwords\nكَرَّةًAnother turn\nبِمَفَازَتِهِمBy attaining salvation\nمَقَالِيدُThe keys of all treasures\nلَيَحبَطَنَّBecome worthless\nقَبضَتُهُHis grip\nمَطوِيَّاتٌRolled up in His Right Hand"],[466,"§Az-Zumar\ndeeds\nPerform your prayer today in a perfect way, so Allah will ease your standing before Him in the Hereafter.\nIn order to help remove arrogance from your soul, try a humbling experience today, such as sitting with poor workers, sharing food with them or inviting them over to your house.\nDo different acts of worship today, such as performing a prayer, fasting, and giving for charity, so you may enter through Paradise’s gates that are designated for these deeds.\nguid\nOn the Day of Resurrection, every servant will be paid in full for what he has done.\nBeware of turning away and abandoning the caller to good.\nMaintain purity inwardly and outwardly, purity of your food and clothing, so you may hear this on the Day of Resurrection:\nrefl\nوَأَشۡرَقَتِ ٱلۡأَرۡضُ بِنُورِ رَبِّهَا\nFrom this, it is known that the existing lights will have vanished and disappeared on the Day of Resurrection. And this will indeed be the case, for Allah has told us that the sun will be rolled up, the moon will be darkened, the stars will be scattered, and the people will be left in darkness. At that point the earth will be illuminated with the light of its Lord, when He manifests Himself and descends to pass judgement among them. On that day, Allah will give people extra strength and will recreate them in such a way that they will be able to withstand His light and it will not burn them. They will also be enabled to see Him, otherwise His light is immense, and if it were to be made manifest, the glory of His Countenance would burn all of His creation, as far as He sees. Al-Saadi: 730.\nWhat proves that people will be first gathered in darkness? How to reconcile between this verse and the Prophetic Hadiths that indicate Allah’s light burns all of His creation, as far as He sees?\nوَجِاْيٓءَ بِٱلنَّبِيِّۧنَ وَٱلشُّهَدَآءِ وَقُضِيَ بَيۡنَهُم بِٱلۡحَقِّ وَهُمۡ لَا يُظۡلَمُونَ ٦٩\nThe Prophets will be brought to be asked about the response they received from their people. The witnesses will be the martyrs who were killed in the cause of Allah; they will testify on the Day of Resurrection for those who defended the religion of Allah. Al-Qurtubi: 18/315.\nWhy will the Prophets and witnesses be brought on that distressing Day?\nوَسِيقَ ٱلَّذِينَ كَفَرُوٓاْ إِلَىٰ جَهَنَّمَ زُمَرًاۖ حَتَّىٰٓ إِذَا جَآءُوهَا فُتِحَتۡ أَبۡوَٰبُهَا\nAllah begins by relating what will happen to those who deserve punishment, since it is more important at this point, as it re-admonishes and intimidates those who did not take heed of repeated admonishments in the Quran like this one. As for those who will be rewarded, they attained the intended objective, and what is mentioned about them is reiterating the glad tidings and praise for them. Ibn Ashur: 24/69.\nAllah begins by relating what will happen to those who deserve punishment. Why?\nوَسِيقَ ٱلَّذِينَ كَفَرُوٓاْ إِلَىٰ جَهَنَّمَ زُمَرًاۖ حَتَّىٰٓ إِذَا جَآءُوهَا فُتِحَتۡ أَبۡوَٰبُهَا\nThey will be divided into groups commensurate with the levels of their disbelief. If the disbelievers of Quraish are meant here, then, they will vary based on the intensity of their disbelief, and their display of kindness or harshness toward the Muslims. Ibn Ashur: 24/69.\nThe disbelievers will be divided into groups when they are driven to Hell. Why?\nوَسِيقَ ٱلَّذِينَ ٱتَّقَوۡاْ رَبَّهُمۡ إِلَى ٱلۡجَنَّةِ زُمَرًاۖ\nThey will be divided into groups commensurate with the levels of their righteousness. Ibn Ashur: 24/71.\nThose who feared their Lord will be driven to Paradise in groups. Why?\nوَسِيقَ ٱلَّذِينَ ٱتَّقَوۡاْ رَبَّهُمۡ إِلَى ٱلۡجَنَّةِ زُمَرًاۖ\nFor both parties, Allah says the same, (will be driven). Driving the people of Fire by pushing them toward it in humiliation and disgrace, similar to what is done to the captives and outlaws when taken to imprisonment or execution. Driving the people of Paradise, however, will be escorting their carriages to the place of honor and pleasure, since they will be carried to Paradise, similar to what is done for dignitaries when coming to visit a king. What a difference between driving each party. Al-Qurtubi: 18/3.\nIs there a difference between driving the people of Fire and the people of Paradise?\nحَتَّىٰٓ إِذَا جَآءُوهَا وَفُتِحَتۡ أَبۡوَٰبُهَا وَقَالَ لَهُمۡ خَزَنَتُهَا سَلَٰمٌ عَلَيۡكُمۡ طِبۡتُمۡ فَٱدۡخُلُوهَا خَٰلِدِينَ ٧٣\n(Until, when they reach it): This is a conditional sentence with an omitted result. What it implies is that when they come to the gates of Paradise, they will be opened for them as a sign of honor, and the angelic keepers will meet them with glad tidings, greetings of peace and praise. Unlike the keepers of Hell who will meet the disbelievers with rebuke and reprimand. The believers will be filled with happiness and joy, each according to his degree of luxury and delights. What happens after this is not mentioned; it is left for the imagination to think of its dearest wishes and be filled with hope. Ibn Kathir: 4/68.\nIn this verse, the result of the conditional sentence is omitted. Why?\nwords\nوَنُفِخَThe first blow in the Horn that will cause death to all created beings\nفَصَعِقَWill fall dead\nزُمَرًاGroups\nفَبِئسَWretched\nطِبتُمYou have become pure\nنَتَبَوَّأُWe settle in"],[467,"§Az-Zumar, Ghafir\ndeeds\nSay, \"O Allah, grant me a good outcome on all of my affairs, and save me from the disgrace in this world, and the torment in the Hereafter.\"\nWhen you recite: [The Forgiver of sin and Accepter of repentance], say, \"O Forgiver of sin, forgive my sin; O Accepter of repentance, accept my repentance.\"\nRead a book to familiarize yourself with the attributes and functions of angels.\nguid\nAllah's greatness manifests through His Names: the All-Mighty, the All-Knowing, the Forgiver of sin and Accepter of repentance, the Severe in punishment and Infinite in bounty.\nBeware of becoming deceived by the adornments of life that are given to the enemies of Islam.\nNever argue using falsehood, rather always aim for the truth.\nrefl\nوَقِيلَ ٱلۡحَمۡدُ لِلَّهِ رَبِّ ٱلۡعَٰلَمِينَ ٧٥\nThe sentence is in passive voice to indicate that everyone praises Allah for His judgment. The dwellers of heavens and earth, the righteous and the wicked, and mankind and jinn, even the inhabitants of the Fire. It is as if the whole universe utters praise to Him. Ibn Al-Qayim: 2/403.\nIn this verse, the sentence is in passive voice. Why?\nوَقِيلَ ٱلۡحَمۡدُ لِلَّهِ رَبِّ ٱلۡعَٰلَمِينَ ٧٥\nMeaning: All of creation, whether animate or inanimate, will speak words of praise to Allah, the Lord of all that exists, for His wisdom and justice. These words are not attributed to any specific speaker, which indicates that the whole of creation will testify to His praise. Ibn Kathir: 4/70.\nIn this verse, the sentence begins with (it will be said) not \"they said\", why?\nتَنزِيلُ ٱلۡكِتَٰبِ مِنَ ٱللَّهِ ٱلۡعَزِيزِ ٱلۡعَلِيمِ ٢\nHere, the use of Allah's attributes, (the All-Mighty, the All-Knowing) alludes to the fact that those who deny that this Book was revealed by Allah, will be defeated and overpowered, and that Allah knows and will hold them accountable for what they hide in their hearts. Moreover, the Quran is referred to as the word of the All-Mighty, the All-Knowing, hence, no one other than Allah is able or knowledgeable to produce the like of it. Ibn Ashur: 24/79\nThe verse ends with (the All-Mighty, the All-Knowing). Why?\nغَافِرِ ٱلذَّنۢبِ وَقَابِلِ ٱلتَّوۡبِ شَدِيدِ ٱلۡعِقَابِ\nIt is like this verse, (Inform My servants that I am indeed the All-Forgiving, the Most Merciful ` And that My punishment is the most painful punishment) [15:49-50]. These two attributes (mercy and punishment) are often mentioned together in the Quran, so that people will remain in a state of both hope and fear. Ibn Kathir: 4/71.\nIn this and other verses, mercy and punishment are often mentioned together. Why?\nغَافِرِ ٱلذَّنۢبِ وَقَابِلِ ٱلتَّوۡبِ\nAllah will grant the repentant sinner two mercies: He will accept his repentance and turn it into an act of obedience and expiates his sins from which he repented and regretted so that he will be as if he never committed them, and that is a bounty from Allah. Ibn Ashur: 24/80.\nThis attribute (Accepter of repentance) is mentioned with (the Forgiver of sin). Why?\nمَا يُجَٰدِلُ فِيٓ ءَايَٰتِ ٱللَّهِ إِلَّا ٱلَّذِينَ كَفَرُواْ فَلَا يَغۡرُرۡكَ تَقَلُّبُهُمۡ فِي ٱلۡبِلَٰدِ ٤\n(So do not be deceived by their movements in the land), means: O Muhammad, do not be deceived by their disposition and dwelling in the land despite their disbelief in their Lord, and think that they were given respite because they may have some truth. We did not give them respite because of that, rather, until their prescribed time comes, and the decree of punishment will come to pass against them. Al-Tabari: 21/352.\nAllah gives respite to the disbelievers despite their persistence on disbelief. Why?\nٱلَّذِينَ يَحۡمِلُونَ ٱلۡعَرۡشَ وَمَنۡ حَوۡلَهُۥ يُسَبِّحُونَ بِحَمۡدِ رَبِّهِمۡ وَيُؤۡمِنُونَ بِهِۦ\nIf it is said: What is the use of saying, (and believe in Him), while it is well-known that the bearers of the Throne and those around it believe in Allah? The answer is to show the virtue of faith. Ibn Juzay: 2/276.\nWhat is the use of saying, (and believe in Him), even though all angels are believers?\nwords\nحَآفِّينَSurrounding and looking at the Throne\nوَقُضِيَ بَينَهُم بِالحَقّIt will be judged between all created beings in truth\nذِي الطَّولِHe Infinite in bounty\nفَلاَ يَغرُركَDo not be deceived\nلِيُدحِضُواTo refute\nوَقِهِمProtect them"],[468,"§Ghafir\ndeeds\nEnjoin your brothers and your household to perform prayer, in hope that they will join you in Paradise.\nFollow the example of the angels by supplicating Allah for your fellow believers like you do for yourself.\nIdentify some of your sins and shortcomings, then ask Allah to accept your repentance before you will confess to them in the Hereafter but to no avail.\nguid\nSaeed bin Jubair said: When the believer enters Paradise, he will ask for the whereabout of his father, son and brother, and it will be said: They did not reach your rank in righteousness. He will say: I have done righteous deeds to benefit myself and them; hence, they will be joined with him in the same rank. Then, Saeed bin Jubair recited this verse:\nKnow that the most exalted mercy attained by the servant is for Allah to save him from the evil consequences of his sins.\nNever mind the disbelievers' anger at you when you do what pleases Allah.\nrefl\nرَبَّنَا وَأَدۡخِلۡهُمۡ جَنَّٰتِ عَدۡنٍ ٱلَّتِي وَعَدتَّهُمۡ وَمَن صَلَحَ مِنۡ ءَابَآئِهِمۡ وَأَزۡوَٰجِهِمۡ وَذُرِّيَّٰتِهِمۡۚ إِنَّكَ أَنتَ ٱلۡعَزِيزُ ٱلۡحَكِيمُ ٨\nThis indicates that joining spouses, offspring, and companions is a source of joy, and the basis for good things coming to the believers from other than their deeds, similar to the angels’ supplication for the believers, the righteous from among their parents, their spouses and their offspring. Al-Saadi: 733.\nThis verse exhorts the believers to befriend righteous people. Explain.\nرَبَّنَا وَأَدۡخِلۡهُمۡ جَنَّٰتِ عَدۡنٍ ٱلَّتِي وَعَدتَّهُمۡ وَمَن صَلَحَ مِنۡ ءَابَآئِهِمۡ وَأَزۡوَٰجِهِمۡ وَذُرِّيَّٰتِهِمۡۚ\nMeaning: Bring them together so that they may find delight in one another in closer dwellings. Ibn Kathir: 4/74.\nParents, spouses and offspring are singled out for mention. Why?\nإِنَّكَ أَنتَ ٱلۡعَزِيزُ ٱلۡحَكِيمُ ٨\n(The Almighty) Who subjugates all things. By Your might, You forgive their sins, relieve them of hardships and cause them to attain all that is good. (the All-Wise) Who does what is appropriate. So, we do not ask You, O our Lord, for anything contrary to that which is dictated by Your wisdom; rather, part of Your wisdom - as You have told us on the lips of Your Messengers, and as dictated by Your grace - is to forgive the believers. Al-Saadi: 732.\nThe verse ends with (the All-Mighty, the All-Wise), why?\nإِنَّ ٱلَّذِينَ كَفَرُواْ يُنَادَوۡنَ لَمَقۡتُ ٱللَّهِ أَكۡبَرُ مِن مَّقۡتِكُمۡ أَنفُسَكُمۡ إِذۡ تُدۡعَوۡنَ إِلَى ٱلۡإِيمَٰنِ فَتَكۡفُرُونَ ١٠\nAbhorrence: Hatred that is due to a sin or disgrace, and the disbelievers will experience this situation when they enter the Fire. They will hate themselves, i.e. each other, or everyone will hate himself. Then, the angels will call them, saying: Allah's abhorrence of you in worldly life due to your disbelief was greater than your abhorrence of yourselves today. Ibn Juzay: 2/277.\nThe disbelievers will hate themselves when they enter the Fire. How?\nقَالُواْ رَبَّنَآ أَمَتَّنَا ٱثۡنَتَيۡنِ وَأَحۡيَيۡتَنَا ٱثۡنَتَيۡنِ فَٱعۡتَرَفۡنَا بِذُنُوبِنَا فَهَلۡ إِلَىٰ خُرُوجٖ مِّن سَبِيلٖ ١١\n(You have caused us to die twice and brought us to life twice), this is a full admission of resurrection, hoping to rid themselves of Allah’s abhorrence when they were invited to Islam, but they disbelieved. Some may ask: How is saying: (Our Lord, You have caused us to die twice and brought us to life twice) becomes a confession of their sins? The answer is: They used to deny the resurrection, but when they saw dying and coming back to life were repeated, they realized Allah’s capability to resurrect, hence, they confessed their sins, which were denying resurrection and what it entailed of sins, since he who does not believe in the Hereafter is indifferent to committing sins. Ibn Juzay: 2/278.\nCorruption of belief is a cause for committing sins. Explain in light of this verse.\nيُلۡقِي ٱلرُّوحَ مِنۡ أَمۡرِهِۦ عَلَىٰ مَن يَشَآءُ مِنۡ عِبَادِهِۦ\n(He places the inspiration): He sends down the revelation. In the Arabic text, the word (Rūh), which means \"spirit\" is used to indicate that the revelation gives life to people's hearts. Al-Baghawi: 4/38.\nThe revelation is called (Rūh). Why?\nيُلۡقِي ٱلرُّوحَ مِنۡ أَمۡرِهِۦ عَلَىٰ مَن يَشَآءُ مِنۡ عِبَادِهِۦ لِيُنذِرَ يَوۡمَ ٱلتَّلَاقِ ١٥\n(The Day of Meeting), the Day of Resurrection, and it is called as such because all created beings will meet on it, or, because the inhabitants of the heavens meet those of the earth. Moreover, it is said that it is because all created beings will meet with their Lord. Ibn Juzay: 2/278.\nWhat is the Day of Meeting? Why is it called as such?\nwords\nلَمَقتُ اللهِAbhorrence\nيُنِيبُTurns back in repentance\nيَومَ التَّلاَقِThe Day when the former and later peoples meet\nبَارِزُونَThey will be brought forth before their Lord"],[469,"§Ghafir\ndeeds\nRecall someone whom you wronged against, and ask him to forgive you, or supplicate Allah for him in his absence, and ask for Allah's forgiveness.\nPreserve the purity of your heart today by not peeping at what is unlawful for you in the street, market, television, computer, or mobile phone.\nRecall minutes that you spent in heedlessness or a sin, and spend the same amount of time looking at the verses of the Quran, so good deeds may wipe out misdeeds.\nguid\nNo one will be wronged on the Day of Resurrection by an increase in his misdeeds, or a reduction in his good deeds.\nThe hearts will reach the throats on the Day of Resurrection due to its immensity and terror.\nSome people observe the ruins of past nations for leisure and pastime, and do not reflect on their punishment, as Allah commands them to.\nrefl\nإِنَّ ٱللَّهَ سَرِيعُ ٱلۡحِسَابِ ١٧\nSince Allah is the All-Knowing Whose nothing will be absent from His knowledge, He will not delay recompensing one person to engage another. Just like He provides them all with their provisions in one instant, He will bring them to account in one instant. Al-Qurtubi: 18/341.\nExplain Allah's greatness in bringing His servants to account swiftly.\nوَأَنذِرۡهُمۡ يَوۡمَ ٱلۡأٓزِفَةِ إِذِ ٱلۡقُلُوبُ لَدَى ٱلۡحَنَاجِرِ\n(The Approaching Day), it is called as such because it is near, as every awaited event is near. (When hearts are at the throats): The hearts will move away from their places due to intense fear until they reach their throats. Then, they will not move back to their places, nor exit out of their mouths so they may die and rest. Al-Baghawi: 4/39.\nWhy is the Day of Resurrection called the Approaching Day? How will the hearts reach the throats?\nيَعۡلَمُ خَآئِنَةَ ٱلۡأَعۡيُنِ وَمَا تُخۡفِي ٱلصُّدُورُ ١٩\nAllah describes His complete knowledge which encompasses all things, great and small, major and minor, so that people will take note that He knows about them, and they will have the proper sense of shyness before Allah, will fear Him as He should be feared, and will pay attention to the fact that He can see them. Ibn Kathir: 4/77.\nThe Muslim learns a practical lesson from this verse. What is it?\nيَعۡلَمُ خَآئِنَةَ ٱلۡأَعۡيُنِ وَمَا تُخۡفِي ٱلصُّدُورُ ١٩\nIbn Abbas (k) said: This verse refers to a man who sits among others, and when a woman passes by, he sneakily glances at her. Moreover, Ibn Abbas said: This refers to a man who looks at a woman, and when his companions see him, he lowers his gaze, but Allah knows that he wishes to have looked at her private part. (And what the hearts conceal), Ibn Abbas said: It means that if they were alone together, will he commit adultery with her or not? Al-Qurtubi: 18/343.\nWhat are the sneaky glances? What do the hearts conceal?\nوَلَقَدۡ أَرۡسَلۡنَا مُوسَىٰ بِـَٔايَٰتِنَا وَسُلۡطَٰنٖ مُّبِينٍ ٢٣\nAllah relates the story of Moses and Pharaoh to His Messenger (ﷺ) to console, comfort, and teach him that with the trial, no matter how intense, comes relief, and that Allah will give him victory over his people, like He had given victory to Moses over Pharaoh and his people. Al-Jaza'iri: 4/527.\nHow is the story of Moses and Pharaoh relevant to the preceding verses?\nإِلَىٰ فِرۡعَوۡنَ وَهَٰمَٰنَ وَقَٰرُونَ فَقَالُواْ سَٰحِرٞ كَذَّابٞ ٢٤ فَلَمَّا جَآءَهُم بِٱلۡحَقِّ مِنۡ عِندِنَا قَالُواْ ٱقۡتُلُوٓاْ أَبۡنَآءَ ٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُواْ مَعَهُۥ وَٱسۡتَحۡيُواْ نِسَآءَهُمۡۚ وَمَا كَيۡدُ ٱلۡكَٰفِرِينَ إِلَّا فِي ضَلَٰلٖ ٢٥\nThese three men decided and agreed to the killing of the sons of the Children of Israel, the strong youth among them, who followed Moses, while keeping the women as servants and slaves. (But, the plots of the disbelievers are always bound to fail): This is a brief statement indicating that Allah has foiled the plot of these three men, and they were not able to kill any of the Children of Israel, and their pursuit failed, rather, Allah impeded their pursuit and plots. Ibn Atiyah: 4/554.\nAllah's Will is above that of the kings. Explain in light of these two verses.\nفَلَمَّا جَآءَهُم بِٱلۡحَقِّ مِنۡ عِندِنَا قَالُواْ ٱقۡتُلُوٓاْ أَبۡنَآءَ ٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُواْ مَعَهُۥ وَٱسۡتَحۡيُواْ نِسَآءَهُمۡۚ وَمَا كَيۡدُ ٱلۡكَٰفِرِينَ إِلَّا فِي ضَلَٰلٖ ٢٥\nReflect on this point which is often repeated in the Book of Allah: If the context is a specific story or a specific matter, and Allah wants to give a ruling concerning that specific matter but not specific to that matter, He mentions the ruling and connects it to the general reason for that ruling to make it more general in application, which includes the story mentioned in that context too to ward off any mistaken notion that the ruling is limited only to that specific instance. Hence, Allah does not say here “their plot was bound to fail\"; rather, He says: (The plots of the disbelievers are bound to fail). Al-Saadi: 736.\nThe verse ends with a general statement, (The plots of the disbelievers are bound to fail), and does not end with \"their plot was bound to fail\", or \"Pharaoh's plot was bound to fail\". Why?\nwords\nيَومَ الآزِفَةِThe Approaching Resurrection Day\nلَدَى الحَنَاجِرِTheir hearts are at their throats due to extreme anguish\nكَاظِمِينَFilled with distress and sorrow\nخَائِنَةَ الأَعيُنِGlances of the eyes at what is prohibited\nوَاقٍA protector"],[470,"§Ghafir\ndeeds\nWhen you become frightened of a criminal, say, \"O Allah, we seek refuge with You against their evils, and we make You our shield against them.\"\nFollowing the example of the believer from Pharaoh's house, defend, through a message or talk, a scholar or a preacher whom foolish people ridicule.\nSeek refuge with Allah from transgression, lying, and arrogance.\nguid\nThe record of the talker is an indication of his truthfulness or falsehood.\nAllah, the Almighty, is the ultimate refuge for the believer from all fears.\nThe farthest person from true guidance is one who transgressed in sins, and claimed that Allah enjoined them.\nrefl\nوَقَالَ فِرۡعَوۡنُ ذَرُونِيٓ أَقۡتُلۡ مُوسَىٰ وَلۡيَدۡعُ رَبَّهُۥٓۖ إِنِّيٓ أَخَافُ أَن يُبَدِّلَ دِينَكُمۡ أَوۡ أَن يُظۡهِرَ فِي ٱلۡأَرۡضِ ٱلۡفَسَادَ ٢٦\nPharaoh's conceitedness and short-sightedness in evaluating matters led him to believe that anything contrary to their religion is considered corruption, for they did not have any proof for their religion except habit and worldly gain. Ibn Ashur: 24/125.\nThe corrupt habits of the fathers and grandfathers prevent people from guidance. Explain.\nوَقَالَ مُوسَىٰٓ إِنِّي عُذۡتُ بِرَبِّي وَرَبِّكُم مِّن كُلِّ مُتَكَبِّرٖ لَّا يُؤۡمِنُ بِيَوۡمِ ٱلۡحِسَابِ ٢٧\nWhoever does not truly believe in the Day of Reckoning, will not anticipate a reward for his good deed, nor will he be afraid of punishment for his evil deeds. Al-Tabari: 21/375.\nWhy did Moses (u) seek refuge with Allah from one who did not believe in the Day of Reckoning in particular?\nوَقَالَ رَجُلٞ مُّؤۡمِنٞ مِّنۡ ءَالِ فِرۡعَوۡنَ يَكۡتُمُ إِيمَٰنَهُۥٓ أَتَقۡتُلُونَ رَجُلًا أَن يَقُولَ رَبِّيَ ٱللَّهُ وَقَدۡ جَآءَكُم بِٱلۡبَيِّنَٰتِ مِن رَّبِّكُمۡۖ\nAllah praises a man from the house of Pharaoh who concealed his faith, mentions him in His Book, and keeps his record in the Quran for words that he said in a sitting place of disbelief. How does he compare to Omar bin Al-Khattab (t) who waved his sword in Makkah, and said: \"By Allah, I will never worship Allah in secret after today.\"Ibn Atiyah: 4/555.\nThis verse indicates the virtues of the Prophet’s Companions. Explain.\nوَإِن يَكُ كَٰذِبٗا فَعَلَيۡهِ كَذِبُهُۥۖ وَإِن يَكُ صَادِقٗا يُصِبۡكُم بَعۡضُ ٱلَّذِي يَعِدُكُمۡ\nThis saying from the believer was not because he doubted Moses’ mission and truthfulness, rather, he meant to make his point softly without provoking their evil actions. Al-Qurtubi: 18/348-349.\nDid the believer say what he said because he doubted Moses’ (u) truthfulness? What etiquette we may learn from this approach?\nوَإِن يَكُ صَادِقٗا يُصِبۡكُم بَعۡضُ ٱلَّذِي يَعِدُكُمۡ\nHe said, (some) and not \"all\", even though what will befall them is all that which he threatened them with, in order to be gentle with them in speech, guard against the notion of siding with Moses, and demonstrate his sincere advice to Pharaoh and his people hoping that they would accept the truth. Ibn Juzay: 2/280.\nThe believer said, (some of what he is threatening you with), even though what will befall them is all that which he threatened them with. Why?\nوَقَالَ ٱلَّذِيٓ ءَامَنَ يَٰقَوۡمِ إِنِّيٓ أَخَافُ عَلَيۡكُم مِّثۡلَ يَوۡمِ ٱلۡأَحۡزَابِ ٣٠\nRepeating his call to his people, without despairing of their ever being guided - which is the way of those who call people to Allah; they keep on calling people to their Lord and nothing deters them from that, for the arrogance of those whom they called does not deter them from persisting in calling them. Al-Saadi: 737.\nThis verse has noble guidance to those who call others to Allah to not despair. Explain.\nوَيَٰقَوۡمِ إِنِّيٓ أَخَافُ عَلَيۡكُمۡ يَوۡمَ ٱلتَّنَادِ ٣٢\nOn the Day of Resurrection, every people will be called together with their leader, and they will call out to each other. The people of Paradise will call out to the people of Hellfire, and the people of Hellfire will call out to the people of Paradise. The people of the Elevations will be called. Some people will be called among the wretched, and others will be called among the blissful; so-and-so will be in bliss where he will never see wretchedness ever, and so-and-so will be in wretchedness where he will never see bliss ever. When death is slaughtered, it will be called: \"O people of Paradise! Eternity for you and no death, O people of Hell! Eternity for you and no death.\" Al-Baghawi: 4/42.\nThe Day of Resurrection is called the Day of Calling. Why?\nwords\nعُذتُI sought refuge\nظَاهِرِينَDominant in the land\nيَومَ التَّنَادِDay of Resurrection when people cry out to one another\nمُدبِرِينَYou will turn your backs fleeing\nعَاصِمٍA protector"],[471,"§Ghafir\ndeeds\nSeek refuge with Allah from arguing without knowledge and from Allah's abhorrence.\nFollowing the example of the righteous of former nations, call to Allah a heedless person with wisdom and good approach.\nDo a righteous deed today that you have never done before in hope that Allah, the Almighty, will let you into Paradise for it.\nguid\nBeware of arguing without knowledge.\nThe beginning of damnation is when your evil deeds are made appealing to you so that you see them good; Allah forbids.\nBe confident in Allah, the Almighty, in His victory, empowerment of His servants, and abandonment of His enemies.\nrefl\nوَلَقَدۡ جَآءَكُمۡ يُوسُفُ مِن قَبۡلُ بِٱلۡبَيِّنَٰتِ فَمَا زِلۡتُمۡ فِي شَكّٖ مِّمَّا جَآءَكُم بِهِۦۖ حَتَّىٰٓ إِذَا هَلَكَ قُلۡتُمۡ لَن يَبۡعَثَ ٱللَّهُ مِنۢ بَعۡدِهِۦ رَسُولٗاۚ كَذَٰلِكَ يُضِلُّ ٱللَّهُ مَنۡ هُوَ مُسۡرِفٞ مُّرۡتَابٌ ٣٤\nHe discerned a little use in advising them, and that they were bent on denying Moses, so he raised the level of admonishing them to placing blame on what had occurred in the past, and reminding them that they were descendants of those who denied Joseph when he came to them with clear proof. Denying those who call them to the truth was well-known in their ancestors, and had become an innate disposition for them. Ibn Ashur: 24/138.\nWhat is the link between this verse and the one before?\nكَبُرَ مَقۡتًا عِندَ ٱللَّهِ وَعِندَ ٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُواْۚ\nSimilarly, His believing servants despise that intensely, in agreement with their Lord. These are the elite of Allah’s creation, and their hatred is indicative of the reprehensible and abhorrent nature of those whom they despise. Al-Saadi: 738.\nHe who is hated by scholars and righteous people is at a great risk, and he has to rectify that. Explain that in light of this verse.\nأَسۡبَٰبَ ٱلسَّمَٰوَٰتِ فَأَطَّلِعَ إِلَىٰٓ إِلَٰهِ مُوسَىٰ وَإِنِّي لَأَظُنُّهُۥ كَٰذِبٗاۚ\nWhen Pharaoh said, in the presence of his eminent ones, (so that I have a look at the God of Moses), his words implied a hint of recognition of (the God of Moses), hence, he worriedly revised that by saying, (for I think he is a liar). Ibn Atiyah: 4/560.\nWhat is the link between the beginning of the verse and Pharaoh’s words: (I think he is a liar)?\nأَسۡبَٰبَ ٱلسَّمَٰوَٰتِ فَأَطَّلِعَ إِلَىٰٓ إِلَٰهِ مُوسَىٰ وَإِنِّي لَأَظُنُّهُۥ كَٰذِبٗاۚ وَكَذَٰلِكَ زُيِّنَ لِفِرۡعَوۡنَ سُوٓءُ عَمَلِهِۦ وَصُدَّ عَنِ ٱلسَّبِيلِۚ وَمَا كَيۡدُ فِرۡعَوۡنَ إِلَّا فِي تَبَابٖ ٣٧\nThis sentence, (for I think he is a liar) is an intervening clause, used by Pharaoh to guards against the notion by Haman and his people that Moses’s message had weakened his faith in his religion and gods; or that he was searching and reflecting on the evidence of true knowledge. He, therefore, assured them that he meant to discredit Moses’s claim through physical evidence. Ibn Ashur: 24/147.\nWhat was the use for Pharaoh to have said: (for I think he is a liar)?\nوَمَا كَيۡدُ فِرۡعَوۡنَ إِلَّا فِي تَبَابٖ ٣٧\nIt is called: The plan, because it was not done for its apparent purpose, rather, it was meant to deceive his people into believing that Moses (u) was a liar. Ibn Ashur: 24/148.\nThe tall building that Pharaoh ordered to be built is called (plan). Why?\nوَمَا كَيۡدُ فِرۡعَوۡنَ إِلَّا فِي تَبَابٖ ٣٧\nPharaoh's deception in wanting to have a look at the God of Moses was not except in ruin, loss of wealth, and complete waste, because he lost all what was spent on that tall building, and did not achieve what he wanted, so, that was the ruin and total loss. Al-Tabari: 21/388.\nWhy is Pharaoh's plan described as (ruin)?\nيَٰقَوۡمِ إِنَّمَا هَٰذِهِ ٱلۡحَيَوٰةُ ٱلدُّنۡيَا مَتَٰعٞ وَإِنَّ ٱلۡأٓخِرَةَ هِيَ دَارُ ٱلۡقَرَارِ ٣٩\nMeaning: The enjoyment of this life is short, then it will cease and perish. (Whereas the Hereafter is the permanent abode), the eternal life in the Hereafter which is either Paradise or Hellfire, since they are imperishable. Al-Qurtubi: 18/361.\nExplain how he called them to Allah by describing the reality of the life of this world.\nwords\nشَكٍّDoubt\nمُرتَابٌSkeptic about Allah\nيَطبَعُHe seals\nصَرحًاA tall building\nتَبَابٍLoss, ruin"],[472,"§Ghafir\ndeeds\nCall a sinner to repentance, or a disbeliever to Islam, and show your compassion and care for him.\nRecall a matter that concerns you, then entrust it to Allah, and He will suffice you.\nVisit the cemetery, then seek refuge with Allah from the punishment in the grave.\nguid\nUse an effective and influencing preaching style when calling others to Allah.\nThe believer from Pharaoh's house made an excellent conclusion to his admonishment and advice to his people.\nThe immense loss will be suffered by the weak-minded who were led in this world and will be disowned in the Hereafter.\nrefl\nوَأُفَوِّضُ أَمۡرِيٓ إِلَى ٱللَّهِۚ إِنَّ ٱللَّهَ بَصِيرُۢ بِٱلۡعِبَادِ ٤٤ فَوَقَىٰهُ ٱللَّهُ سَيِّـَٔاتِ مَا مَكَرُواْۖ\nThis proves that he who entrusts his affairs to Allah, the Glorified and Sublime , Allah will be with him. Ibn Juzay: 2/282.\nWhat is the lesson learned from these two verses for a Muslim?\nفَوَقَىٰهُ ٱللَّهُ سَيِّـَٔاتِ مَا مَكَرُواْۖ\nMeaning: They wanted to afflict him with punishment, but when they searched for him, they could not find him because he entrusted his affairs to Allah. Al-Qurtubi: 18/363.\nWhat happened to the believer from Pharaoh’s house when he entrusted his affairs to Allah?\nوَحَاقَ بِـَٔالِ فِرۡعَوۡنَ سُوٓءُ ٱلۡعَذَابِ ٤٥\nDrowning is an evil punishment, because a drowning person is tormented by having his breath cutoff for an extended period of time, while floating and going down many times, frightened by the immense waves and certain of his death. Then, he is subject to being eaten alive or dead by predators of the sea, thus, it will be torment in this life and cited disgrace by people after death. Ibn Ashur: 24/158.\nWhy is drowning described as an evil punishment?\nٱلنَّارُ يُعۡرَضُونَ عَلَيۡهَا غُدُوّٗا وَعَشِيّٗاۚ وَيَوۡمَ تَقُومُ ٱلسَّاعَةُ أَدۡخِلُوٓاْ ءَالَ فِرۡعَوۡنَ أَشَدَّ ٱلۡعَذَابِ ٤٦\nTheir souls will be exposed to the Fire in the morning and evening until the Day when the Hour begins, and when it does, their bodies and souls will be joined in the Fire. That is why Allah says, (and on the Day when the Hour takes place [it will be said], \"Admit the people of Pharaoh into the most severe punishment\"), the most severe in pain and the greatest shackling. This verse is quoted by Ahl Al-Sunnah as major evidence of the punishment after death in the graves, which is, (The Fire, which they will be exposed to morning and evening). Ibn Kathir: 4/83.\nGiven this verse, how do you infer that punishment on the souls will occur in the graves?\nوَإِذۡ يَتَحَآجُّونَ فِي ٱلنَّارِ فَيَقُولُ ٱلضُّعَفَٰٓؤُاْ لِلَّذِينَ ٱسۡتَكۡبَرُوٓاْ إِنَّا كُنَّا لَكُمۡ تَبَعٗا فَهَلۡ أَنتُم مُّغۡنُونَ عَنَّا نَصِيبٗا مِّنَ ٱلنَّارِ ٤٧\nThis statement by the weak followers to their chiefs has two possible meanings, first: They mean what they say, because during their worldly life, they used to resort to their chiefs in all important matters so they will think that they can do the same for them in this place. Hence, their chiefs, who had been arrogant, will answer them sharing their helplessness and saying, (Indeed, all of us are in it), means, if we are able to save you, we would have saved ourselves. Second: They will say that as a rebuke to their chiefs, which means: You were calling us to the religion of polytheism, which brought us in this punishment, so can you ward off this punishment from us? Ibn Ashur: 24/161.\nIn this verse, what is the purpose of this statement by the weak followers to their chiefs ?\nقَالَ ٱلَّذِينَ ٱسۡتَكۡبَرُوٓاْ إِنَّا كُلّٞ فِيهَآ إِنَّ ٱللَّهَ قَدۡ حَكَمَ بَيۡنَ ٱلۡعِبَادِ ٤٨\nIn this verse, there is a lesson for the heads and leaders of nations. If they imperil themselves and nations while being aware of the consequences, then, they deserve disgrace in this world and multiplied punishment in the Hereafter, as Allah says, (They will certainly bear their own burdens, as well as other burdens along with their own burdens) [29:13]. Moreover, if they pursued headship of their people while being oblivious to the consequences of their incompetence, then, they are blamed for not ascertaining their ability to run the people’s affairs; which leads to acting blindly and resulting in an immense loss for all. Ibn Ashur: 24/163.\nIn this verse, there is a lesson for the heads and leaders. What is it?\nوَقَالَ ٱلَّذِينَ فِي ٱلنَّارِ لِخَزَنَةِ جَهَنَّمَ ٱدۡعُواْ رَبَّكُمۡ يُخَفِّفۡ عَنَّا يَوۡمٗا مِّنَ ٱلۡعَذَابِ ٤٩\nUsing the words, (your Lord) in their speech to the angels is to encourage them to pray for them. Meaning: You are closer to Allah, so He will likely answer your prayer. Thinking that angels’ prayers are more likely to be answered, they ask to lighten for them the punishment for just one day, which is better than reducing the intensity of the Fire from which they ask their chiefs. Ibn Ashur: 24/164.\nWhat is the purpose of using the words, (your Lord) in their speech to the angels?\nwords\nلاَ جَرَمَTruly\nلَيسَ لَهُ دَعوَةٌThey are not worthy of calling upon, nor seeking refuge with since they are helpless\nوَأُفَوِّضُI entrust, hold fast, rely\nوَحَاقَIt surrounded and enveloped\nيَتَحَآجُّونَThey argue\nمُغنُونَAvail, relieve"],[473,"§Ghafir\ndeeds\nRemember the sins you have committed, then ask often for Allah’s forgiveness.\nSay, \"Glory and praise be to Allah,\" a hundred times in the evening and morning.\nSeek refuge with Allah from pride, for it prevents from accepting the truth.\nguid\nBe patient and steadfast in the path of truth, guided by your conviction that Allah's promise is true.\nMost of those who argue with false arguments to refute the truth are arguing based on pride.\nHe Who is capable of creating the great is certainly able to revive the weak.\nrefl\nقَالُوٓاْ أَوَ لَمۡ تَكُ تَأۡتِيكُمۡ رُسُلُكُم بِٱلۡبَيِّنَٰتِۖ قَالُواْ بَلَىٰۚ قَالُواْ فَٱدۡعُواْۗ وَمَا دُعَٰٓؤُاْ ٱلۡكَٰفِرِينَ إِلَّا فِي ضَلَٰلٍ ٥٠\nMeaning: Just as you managed to turn away from the messengers before, manage your affairs today and pray. Ibn Ashur: 24/166.\nTelling the polytheists to pray for themselves is linked to what precedes it. How?\nوَمَا دُعَٰٓؤُاْ ٱلۡكَٰفِرِينَ إِلَّا فِي ضَلَٰلٍ ٥٠\nIt is invalid and worthless because disbelief nullifies all good deeds and prevents any answer to supplication. Al-Saadi: 739.\nMention some of the bad consequences for the disbelievers due to their disbelief.\nإِنَّا لَنَنصُرُ رُسُلَنَا وَٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُواْ فِي ٱلۡحَيَوٰةِ ٱلدُّنۡيَا وَيَوۡمَ يَقُومُ ٱلۡأَشۡهَٰدُ ٥١\nIbn Abbas (k) said: By victory and empowerment. Ad-Dahhak said: By evidence [in this world], and absolution in the Hereafter. Moreover, it is said that by retaliating from the enemies in this world and the Hereafter. All of that had occurred with the Prophets and believers; they were supported by the evidence against those who opposed them. Allah has empowered them over those who fought them, and He avenged their death, similar to what happened with John, the son of Zachariah, when he was killed, seventy thousand were killed to avenge his death. Hence, they are helped by any of these means. Al-Baghawi: 4/47.\nIs victory limited to the Messengers? Is victory limited to overpowering the enemy?\nوَلَقَدۡ ءَاتَيۡنَا مُوسَى ٱلۡهُدَىٰ وَأَوۡرَثۡنَا بَنِيٓ إِسۡرَٰٓءِيلَ ٱلۡكِتَٰبَ ٥٣\nThis is one of the clearest examples of Allah’s help to His Messengers and the believers, and it closely resembles the victory that Allah has decreed for the Prophet (ﷺ) and the believers. By the victory of Moses over the Pharaohs, Allah had given rise to a great nation that no one would consider without such a victory. It was given a great Sharia and kingdom. Similarly, the victory of the Prophet (ﷺ) and the believers was even greater, more thorough, and nobler. Ibn Ashur: 24/169.\nThe story of Moses is one of the clearest examples of Allah’s help to the believers. How?\nإِنَّ ٱلَّذِينَ يُجَٰدِلُونَ فِيٓ ءَايَٰتِ ٱللَّهِ بِغَيۡرِ سُلۡطَٰنٍ أَتَىٰهُمۡ إِن فِي صُدُورِهِمۡ إِلَّا كِبۡرٞ مَّا هُم بِبَٰلِغِيهِۚ\nMeaning: Their arrogance and false pride prevented them from following and obeying you. Ibn Juzay: 2/283.\nWhat was the reason that prevented the disbelievers from following the Prophet (ﷺ)?\nإِنَّ ٱلَّذِينَ يُجَٰدِلُونَ فِيٓ ءَايَٰتِ ٱللَّهِ بِغَيۡرِ سُلۡطَٰنٍ أَتَىٰهُمۡ إِن فِي صُدُورِهِمۡ إِلَّا كِبۡرٞ مَّا هُم بِبَٰلِغِيهِۚ\n(Without evidence), this exception serves as a disparagement of their dispute, as disputing against the signs of Allah can only be done without evidence, because they do not contradict reality. This exception is similar to the exception in this verse, (Who is more astray than one who follows his desire without guidance from Allah) [28:50]. Ibn Ashur: 24/173.\nWhat is the purpose of making exception to the dispute against the signs of Allah?\nوَمَا يَسۡتَوِي ٱلۡأَعۡمَىٰ وَٱلۡبَصِيرُ وَٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُواْ وَعَمِلُواْ ٱلصَّٰلِحَٰتِ وَلَا ٱلۡمُسِيٓءُۚ قَلِيلٗا مَّا تَتَذَكَّرُونَ ٥٨\nThe mention of the blind comes before the seeing, even though sight is nobler than blindness to the same person; moreover, those who are likened to the seeing (the believers) are nobler than those who are likened to the blind (the disbelievers), yet the mention of the like of disbelievers comes first to show the state of those who dispute against the signs of Allah, since they are the ones aimed by this admonishment. Ibn Ashur: 24/178.\nThe mention of the blind comes before the seeing, even though the seeing is nobler. Why?\nwords\nالأَشهَادُWitnesses from among angels, Prophets, and believers against the disbelievers\nمَعذِرَتُهُمTheir excuses\nلأِولِي الأَلبَابِPeople of understanding\nبِالعَشِيِّ وَالإِبكَارِAt the end of the day and its beginning\nسُلطَانٍA clear proof\nمَا هُم بِبَالِغِيهِThey will not reach the high status that Allah had given you"],[474,"§Ghafir\ndeeds\nSupplicate Allah often today so you will not be one of those who are too proud to worship Allah.\nDo something today in which you display humility to your Lord.\nSleep early tonight and wake up early to be in accord with the natural disposition upon which Allah has created you.\nguid\nCiting Allah's favors and blessings and encouraging people to be grateful to Him, the Almighty.\nThe Hour is near, what have you prepared for it?\nBe sincere to Allah in all your deeds.\nrefl\nوَقَالَ رَبُّكُمُ ٱدۡعُونِيٓ أَسۡتَجِبۡ لَكُمۡۚ إِنَّ ٱلَّذِينَ يَسۡتَكۡبِرُونَ عَنۡ عِبَادَتِي سَيَدۡخُلُونَ جَهَنَّمَ دَاخِرِينَ ٦٠\n(Those who are too proud to worship Me), they are too arrogant to turn to Me in hope, as the Prophet (ﷺ) Said: \"Allah is angry with the person who does not ask Him.\" As for this Hadith: \"Verily, supplication is worship,\" it means that supplication and turning to Allah in hope is the worship, as supplication is a sign of showing the person's need and humbleness to Allah. Ibn Juzay: 2/284.\nGiven this verse, how do you infer that supplication is worship?\nوَقَالَ رَبُّكُمُ ٱدۡعُونِيٓ أَسۡتَجِبۡ لَكُمۡۚ إِنَّ ٱلَّذِينَ يَسۡتَكۡبِرُونَ عَنۡ عِبَادَتِي سَيَدۡخُلُونَ جَهَنَّمَ دَاخِرِينَ ٦٠\nSufyan Al-Thawri used to say: \"O You Who love most those who ask of You, and O You Who hate most those who do not ask of You, and there is no one like that apart from You, O Lord.\" Similarly; the poet said: Allah hates not to be asked, and the son of Adam hates to be asked. Ibn Kathir: 4/87.\nCompare between asking Allah and asking people.\nإِنَّ ٱلَّذِينَ يَسۡتَكۡبِرُونَ عَنۡ عِبَادَتِي سَيَدۡخُلُونَ جَهَنَّمَ دَاخِرِينَ ٦٠\nThey will be humiliated and despised, suffering a combination of punishment and humiliation, as a requital for their arrogance. Al-Saadi: 741.\nIn light of this verse, discuss the principle of the requital befits the action.\nٱللَّهُ ٱلَّذِي جَعَلَ لَكُمُ ٱلۡأَرۡضَ قَرَارٗا وَٱلسَّمَآءَ بِنَآءٗ\nSince the principle aim of this verse is for people to show gratitude to Allah -as inferred by the phrase (for you)- earth is mentioned before the sky because its benefits are perceivable; the sky is mentioned afterward as opposite things are mentioned together. Ibn Ashur: 24/189.\nThe earth is mentioned before the sky in this verse. Why?\nوَصَوَّرَكُمۡ فَأَحۡسَنَ صُوَرَكُمۡ\nMuqatil said: He created you in the best creation. Ibn Abbas said: The son of Adam was created upright and straight, using his hands for picking things and eating while other creatures pick their food with their mouths. Al-Baghawi: 4/52.\nThe creation of son of Adam has an advantage over other creatures. Explain.\nوَرَزَقَكُم مِّنَ ٱلطَّيِّبَٰتِۚ\nMeaning: Here, (good things) means savory things because it is mentioned in the context of bestowing. When (good things) is mentioned in the context of explaining what is lawful and unlawful, then it means lawful things. Ibn Juzay: 2/284.\nThe phrase (good things) in the Quran has two different meanings. Mention them with explanation.\nوَأُمِرۡتُ أَنۡ أُسۡلِمَ لِرَبِّ ٱلۡعَٰلَمِينَ ٦٦\nMeaning: I submit with humility and subservience to the Lord of the worlds. Al-Qurtubi: 18/378.\nHow does one submit to Allah, the Almighty?\nwords\nلاَ رَيبَ فِيهَاNo doubt about it\nدَاخِرِينَUtterly debased\nلِتَسكُنُواTo rest\nمُبصِرًاBright\nفَأَنَّى تُؤفَكُونَHow are you deluded by not believing?\nيُؤفَكُDeluded"],[475,"§Ghafir\ndeeds\nSeek refuge with Allah from reaching a degraded geriatric old age.\nRead the stories of the Prophets in Sahih Muslim.\nReflect on the situation of a heedless person who is engaged in doing false deeds while rejoicing in them, and thank Allah for keeping you safe.\nguid\nThose who argue to refute the truth will have a horrific gathering on the Last Day.\nWhen wrong exult spreads throughout society, its punishment becomes imminent.\nRefrain patiently from disobeying Allah, bear patiently in His obedience, and endure patiently with His decreed afflictions, as the relief is near.\nrefl\nإِذِ ٱلۡأَغۡلَٰلُ فِيٓ أَعۡنَٰقِهِمۡ وَٱلسَّلَٰسِلُ يُسۡحَبُونَ ٧١\nAlhasan bin Abi Alhasan said: The chains will not be put around the necks of inhabitants of the fire because they may escape the Lord, but to hold them down when the flames push them afloat. Ibn Atiyah: 4/569.\nWhy will chains be put around the necks of the inhabitants of the Fire?\nفِي ٱلۡحَمِيمِ ثُمَّ فِي ٱلنَّارِ يُسۡجَرُونَ ٧٢\nThe meaning here is close to saying: I have ignited the oven. They will enter the fire like wood when put inside the oven. Mujahid said: They will be the fuel for the Fire. Ibn Juzay: 2/285.\nHow can we infer from this verse the risk of disputing concerning the signs of Allah without knowledge?\nثُمَّ قِيلَ لَهُمۡ أَيۡنَ مَا كُنتُمۡ تُشۡرِكُونَ ٧٣ مِن دُونِ ٱللَّهِۖ قَالُواْ ضَلُّواْ عَنَّا بَل لَّمۡ نَكُن نَّدۡعُواْ مِن قَبۡلُ شَيۡـٔٗاۚ كَذَٰلِكَ يُضِلُّ ٱللَّهُ ٱلۡكَٰفِرِينَ ٧٤\n(Then it will be said to them, \"Where are those whom you used to associate as partners) by worshiping your gods and idols, besides Allah, so they may help save you from the affliction and punishment in which you are, for the worshiped must help those who worshiped him. This will be said to rebuke and scold them for what they had done in the worldly life. Al-Tabari: 21/416.\nWhat is the purpose of asking the polytheists about their gods as they are facing punishment?\nثُمَّ قِيلَ لَهُمۡ أَيۡنَ مَا كُنتُمۡ تُشۡرِكُونَ ٧٣\nThe question is presented here to highlight their wrong and scandal at the gathering on the Last Day because they used to say that they worship the idols to intercede for them against Allah's wrath, but when punishment is decreed upon them and they do not find intercessors, they will be reminded of what they used to claim, and will be said, (Where are those whom you used to associate as partners). Ibn Ashur: 24/204.\nWhat is the purpose of the question in this verse?\nذَٰلِكُم بِمَا كُنتُمۡ تَفۡرَحُونَ فِي ٱلۡأَرۡضِ بِغَيۡرِ ٱلۡحَقِّ وَبِمَا كُنتُمۡ تَمۡرَحُونَ ٧٥\nAs a rebuke to them, it will be said: This punishment is for what you used to rejoice in sins. Meaning: The torment in which you are now is because of your displayed rejoice in sins and the abundance of wealth, followers, and health. Al-Qurtubi: 18/383.\nWhat is the reason for their punishment? What lesson do we learn from that?\nذَٰلِكُم بِمَا كُنتُمۡ تَفۡرَحُونَ فِي ٱلۡأَرۡضِ بِغَيۡرِ ٱلۡحَقِّ وَبِمَا كُنتُمۡ تَمۡرَحُونَ ٧٥\nMeaning: You used to exult in the falsehood that you were following. This is a blameworthy kind of joy that is deserving of punishment, unlike the praiseworthy kind of joy of which Allah says, (Say, \"In the grace of Allah and in His mercy - in that let them rejoice\") [10:58]. That refers to rejoicing in beneficial knowledge and righteous deeds. Al-Saadi: 743.\nWhat is the good exultation? What is the blameworthy exultation?\nفَٱصۡبِرۡ إِنَّ وَعۡدَ ٱللَّهِ حَقّٞۚ فَإِمَّا نُرِيَنَّكَ بَعۡضَ ٱلَّذِي نَعِدُهُمۡ أَوۡ نَتَوَفَّيَنَّكَ فَإِلَيۡنَا يُرۡجَعُونَ ٧٧\nMeaning: If We show you some of the punishment that We threaten them with, it will be comforting to your eyes, and if We cause you to die before that, then, they will return to Us, and We will surely exact harsh retribution upon them. Ibn Juzay: 2/286.\nThere is a consolation to the Prophet (ﷺ) in this statement, (whether We show you). Explain.\nwords\nعَلَقَةٍA clinging clot in the womb\nلِتَبلُغُوا أَشُدَّكُمYou reach your age of full strength\nأَنَّى يُصرَفُونَHow can they be turned away?\nيُسجَرُونَThey will be burned in the Fire\nضَلُّوا عَنَّاWe do not see them\nتَمرَحُونَYou used to exult wrongfully\nمَثوَىThe abode"],[476,"§Ghafir\ndeeds\nNarrate a story from the Quran to some of your collogues or brethren.\nPraise Allah and thank Him for making the grazing animals beneficial in many ways.\nReflect on the images of the ruins of people who were punished by Allah, then ask forgiveness for your sins and shortcomings, lest a similar punishment befalls you.\nguid\nIt is imperative to be admonished by Messengers' stories related by Allah.\nThe end result of falsehood will be in loss, no matter how prominent it becomes, or how much people like it.\nTrue religion is based on true revelation, not on innovations and fables.\nrefl\nوَلَكُمۡ فِيهَا مَنَٰفِعُ وَلِتَبۡلُغُواْ عَلَيۡهَا حَاجَةٗ فِي صُدُورِكُمۡ وَعَلَيۡهَا وَعَلَى ٱلۡفُلۡكِ تُحۡمَلُونَ ٨٠\nIn this verse, the benefits refer to what are equivalent to the benefit of eating, as said, (and some of them you eat) such as benefiting from their fur, milk, value, and payment for blood money and dowry. Moreover, benefiting from their hides as shades and mats to sit on, and enjoying their beauty when going out to graze and when coming back to rest. Ibn Ashur: 24/215-216.\nList some of the benefits implied in Allah's saying: (And for you therein are [other] benefits).\nأَفَلَمۡ يَسِيرُواْ فِي ٱلۡأَرۡضِ فَيَنظُرُواْ كَيۡفَ كَانَ عَٰقِبَةُ ٱلَّذِينَ مِن قَبۡلِهِمۡۚ\nIn the sense of contemplating in such a way as to reach the right conclusion, not merely looking heedlessly and carelessly. Al-Saadi: 744.\nWhen is it beneficial to pass by the ruins of people destroyed by Allah? When is it harmful?\nفَلَمَّا جَآءَتۡهُمۡ رُسُلُهُم بِٱلۡبَيِّنَٰتِ فَرِحُواْ بِمَا عِندَهُم مِّنَ ٱلۡعِلۡمِ\nThis is general in application, and includes all kinds of knowledge that are used to oppose the message brought by the Messengers. One of the branches of knowledge that most deserved to be included in this category is the field of philosophy, especially Greek philosophy, on the basis of which many verses of the Quran were rejected. Moreover, it undermined respect for the Quran in people's hearts, regarding its definitive proofs as mere verbal proofs that do not lead to certainty, and giving precedence to the views of foolish people and followers of falsehood over the proofs of the Quran. This is one of the worst ways of distorting the meanings of Allah’s revelations, opposing and contradicting them. Al-Saadi: 744.\nWhen can some branches of knowledge be considered harmful? Discuss that in light of this verse.\nفَلَمَّا جَآءَتۡهُمۡ رُسُلُهُم بِٱلۡبَيِّنَٰتِ فَرِحُواْ بِمَا عِندَهُم مِّنَ ٱلۡعِلۡمِ\nThe pronoun (them) refers to denying nations, and their (knowledge) can be interpreted in several ways, first: Their belief that they would not be resurrected nor would they be held to account. Second: Their knowledge of worldly benefits and earnings. Third: Knowledge of philosophers who disdain Sharia teachings. Ibn Juzay: 2/286.\nThis verse presents evidence that some types of knowledge can be harmful to its owner. Give examples of that.\nفَلَمَّا جَآءَتۡهُمۡ رُسُلُهُم بِٱلۡبَيِّنَٰتِ فَرِحُواْ بِمَا عِندَهُم مِّنَ ٱلۡعِلۡمِ\nIt is called (knowledge) in accordance with their claim, but, in fact, it is ignorance. Al-Qurtubi: 18/55.\nDo these deniers possess real knowledge?\nفَلَمَّا رَأَوۡاْ بَأۡسَنَا قَالُوٓاْ ءَامَنَّا بِٱللَّهِ وَحۡدَهُۥ وَكَفَرۡنَا بِمَا كُنَّا بِهِۦ مُشۡرِكِينَ ٨٤\nAllah describes the situation of some disbelievers who accepted faith after being overwhelmed by punishment, but it did not benefit them. By mentioning that Allah urges the Arabs to hasten to accept the faith and not procrastinate, lest they face a punishment with which no repentance will benefit them. Ibn Atiyah: 4/572.\nWhat is the benefit of informing Quraish that faith will be of no avail when punishment befall them?\nفَلَمۡ يَكُ يَنفَعُهُمۡ إِيمَٰنُهُمۡ لَمَّا رَأَوۡاْ بَأۡسَنَاۖ سُنَّتَ ٱللَّهِ ٱلَّتِي قَدۡ خَلَتۡ فِي عِبَادِهِۦۖ\nMeaning: Allah has decreed that the faith of disbelievers when they face punishment is of no avail to them, and repentance will not be accepted after witnessing the punishment and becoming exposed to the truth. Al-Qurtubi: 18/386.\nThe verse mentions one of Allah's ways with His creation. What is it?\nwords\nقُضِيَ بِالحَقِّJudgment will be passed with justice between the Messengers and their deniers\nحَاجَةً فِي صُدُورِكُمA need that concerns you\nفَمَا أَغنَى عَنهُمIt was of no avail to them\nوَحَاقَSurrounded\nبَأسَنَاOur punishment\nخَلَتPreceded"],[477,"§Fussilat\ndeeds\nAsk Allah, persistently, to reform your heart.\nAsk Allah for forgiveness often today, following the example of your Prophet (ﷺ) who used to ask for forgiveness more than a hundred times a day.\nDonate some of your wealth, and seek refuge in Allah from the temptation of wealth.\nguid\nIt is imperative to learn Arabic for every Muslim who wants to understand the Word of Allah\nWhen preaching to people or advising someone, let your speech include both encouragement and intimidation.\nYour tranquility is in remaining in obedience to Allah and asking often for Allah's Forgiveness, as He has commanded you.\nrefl\nتَنزِيلٞ مِّنَ ٱلرَّحۡمَٰنِ ٱلرَّحِيمِ ٢\nOne of His greatest mercies is the sending down of this Book, which brought know ledge, guidance, light, healing, mercy and much good; it is among the greatest blessings that He has bestowed upon His servants. Al-Saadi: 744.\nDescribe Allah's greatest mercy on this Muslim Ummah.\nكِتَٰبٞ فُصِّلَتۡ ءَايَٰتُهُۥ\nMeaning: The branches under every topic are explained individually. This requires complete explanation, distinguishing between topics, and making facts clear and distinct. Al-Saadi: 744.\nWhat do you learn from Allah's saying, (A Book whose verses have been detailed)?\nبَشِيرٗا وَنَذِيرٗا فَأَعۡرَضَ أَكۡثَرُهُمۡ فَهُمۡ لَا يَسۡمَعُونَ ٤\n(They do not hear): This is a negation of their beneficial hearing. Ibn Atiyah: 5/4.\nWhat kind of hearing is negated from those disbelievers?\nوَقَالُواْ قُلُوبُنَا فِيٓ أَكِنَّةٖ مِّمَّا تَدۡعُونَآ إِلَيۡهِ وَفِيٓ ءَاذَانِنَا وَقۡرٞ وَمِنۢ بَيۡنِنَا وَبَيۡنِكَ حِجَابٞ فَٱعۡمَلۡ إِنَّنَا عَٰمِلُونَ ٥\nThis barrier was the difference in religion; theirs was worshiping idols while Muhammad’s (ﷺ) religion is worshiping only Allah Who has no partners, and that was the barrier they claimed to have existed between them and the Prophet of Allah. Al-Tabari: 21/429.\nThe disbelievers claimed that a barrier existed between them and the Messenger. What was it?\nقُلۡ إِنَّمَآ أَنَا۠ بَشَرٞ مِّثۡلُكُمۡ يُوحَىٰٓ إِلَيَّ أَنَّمَآ إِلَٰهُكُمۡ إِلَٰهٞ وَٰحِدٞ فَٱسۡتَقِيمُوٓاْ إِلَيۡهِ وَٱسۡتَغۡفِرُوهُۗ وَوَيۡلٞ لِّلۡمُشۡرِكِينَ ٦\nMeaning: I am not an angel, I am from the sons of Adam. Alhasan said: Allah teaches him modesty. Al-Qurtubi: 18/392.\nFrom this verse, show the importance of modesty.\nٱلَّذِينَ لَا يُؤۡتُونَ ٱلزَّكَوٰةَ وَهُم بِٱلۡأٓخِرَةِ هُمۡ كَٰفِرُونَ ٧\nIf you say: From among the traits of the polytheists, why is withholding zakah combined with disbelieving in the Hereafter? I say: Because wealth is the most beloved thing to a man, and it is called: The soul's twin. So, if he spends in the cause of Allah, that becomes the strongest evidence of his firm belief, true intention, and inner purity, as indicated by this verse, (And the likeness of those who spend their wealth, seeking the pleasure of Allah and making firm their own souls)[2:265], they make firm their own souls and prove it by spending out of their wealth. Al-Qurtubi: 18/393.\nWhy is withholding zakah combined with disbelieving in the Hereafter?\n۞قُلۡ أَئِنَّكُمۡ لَتَكۡفُرُونَ بِٱلَّذِي خَلَقَ ٱلۡأَرۡضَ فِي يَوۡمَيۡنِ وَتَجۡعَلُونَ لَهُۥٓ أَندَادٗاۚ ذَٰلِكَ رَبُّ ٱلۡعَٰلَمِينَ ٩ وَجَعَلَ فِيهَا رَوَٰسِيَ مِن فَوۡقِهَا وَبَٰرَكَ فِيهَا وَقَدَّرَ فِيهَآ أَقۡوَٰتَهَا فِيٓ أَرۡبَعَةِ أَيَّامٖ سَوَآءٗ لِّلسَّآئِلِينَ ١٠\nThe wisdom behind creating all these creatures over extended periods of time even though Allah is capable of creating them at once, in order to teach His servants prudence and deliberation. Ibn Atiyah: 5/5.\nWhat is the wisdom behind creating all these creatures over extended periods of time even though Allah is capable of creating them at once?\nwords\nفُصِّلَتIts verses have been detailed and explained\nأَكِنَّةٍCovers keep us from understanding you\nوَقرٌDeafness\nفَاستَقِيمُوا إِلَيهِSeek the straight path to Him\nغَيرُ مَمنُونٍNever ends nor is interrupted\nأَندَادًاPartners, rivals\nرَوَاسِيَFirm mountains\nأَقوَاتَهَاSustenance for its inhabitants"],[478,"§Fussilat\ndeeds\nRead or inquire about the causes of the demise of one of the past nations.\nSeek refuge with Allah from conceit and arrogance.\nWhen you see a strong wind coming, say, \"O Allah, I ask you of its goodness, the goodness within it, and the goodness with which it has been sent; and I seek Your refuge from its harm, the harm within it, and the harm with which it has been sent.\"\nguid\nBeware of turning away from obedience of Allah, for it is the cause of punishment.\nNo disaster without committed sins\nBefore punishing someone, inform him of the sin for which he deserved the punishment.\nrefl\nإِذۡ جَآءَتۡهُمُ ٱلرُّسُلُ مِنۢ بَيۡنِ أَيۡدِيهِمۡ وَمِنۡ خَلۡفِهِمۡ أَلَّا تَعۡبُدُوٓاْ إِلَّا ٱللَّهَۖ قَالُواْ لَوۡ شَآءَ رَبُّنَا لَأَنزَلَ مَلَٰٓئِكَةٗ فَإِنَّا بِمَآ أُرۡسِلۡتُم بِهِۦ كَٰفِرُونَ ١٤\n(Before them and after them): This is a depiction of how eager their Messengers were for their guidance, where each one of them did not leave any means to convey the Message to them but resorted to. Hence, this is likened to someone who approaches another from his front once and from his back another, where he tries to get his attention from all directions, similar to someone who diligently pursues something, so he tracks its whereabouts. Ibn Ashur: 24/253.\nGiven this verse, describe the keenness of the Messengers to convey their Message.\nقَالُواْ لَوۡ شَآءَ رَبُّنَا لَأَنزَلَ مَلَٰٓئِكَةٗ فَإِنَّا بِمَآ أُرۡسِلۡتُم بِهِۦ كَٰفِرُونَ ١٤\nThis specious argument is still in circulation among the disbelievers, handed down from one generation to the next. But it is one of the flimsiest of specious arguments because it is not required for the messenger who is sent to be an angel; rather it is required that the messenger should bring proof of his truthfulness. Therefore, let them bring evidence, if they can, to undermine the sincerity of the messengers by rational or textual proof. But they will never be able to find a way to do that. Al-Saadi: 746.\nGiven this verse, show the similarities between the arguments of the disbelievers.\nفَأَمَّا عَادٞ فَٱسۡتَكۡبَرُواْ فِي ٱلۡأَرۡضِ بِغَيۡرِ ٱلۡحَقِّ وَقَالُواْ مَنۡ أَشَدُّ مِنَّا قُوَّةًۖ\nWhen their Messenger threatened them with punishment, they were deluded by their physical strength, and said: \"We can ward off the punishment with our strength,\" because they had tall and big bodies. Al-Qurtubi: 18/401.\nWhen Allah's punishment approached them, Hūd's people were deluded by something. What was it? Did that benefit them?\nوَأَمَّا ثَمُودُ فَهَدَيۡنَٰهُمۡ\nThe reason why Allah specifically points out that He showed them the path of guidance, even though in the case of other doomed nations proof was established against them and guidance was shown to them, is that the sign given to Thamud was exceptionally clear and was seen by all of them, young and old, male and female. It was a clear sign, hence, that miracle gave them clearer proof and guidance. Al-Saadi: 747.\nAllah specifically points out that He showed Thamud the path of guidance, even though He did the same for all people. Why?\nوَأَمَّا ثَمُودُ فَهَدَيۡنَٰهُمۡ فَٱسۡتَحَبُّواْ ٱلۡعَمَىٰ عَلَى ٱلۡهُدَىٰ\nThis is similar to the present situation of Jews and Christians who live among us, where the Sharia of Islam is made clear to them, but they turn away, so this is preferring blindness over guidance. Ibn Atiyah: 5/10.\nWhat is meant by preferring blindness over guidance in this verse?\nوَيَوۡمَ يُحۡشَرُ أَعۡدَآءُ ٱللَّهِ إِلَى ٱلنَّارِ فَهُمۡ يُوزَعُونَ ١٩\nThey will be pushed and driven to Hellfire. Qatadah and As-Suddi said: \"Their front rows will be held until their last rows join with them.\" Abu Al-Ahwas said: \"When their count is complete, the worst criminals among them will be taken first.\" Al-Qurtubi: 18/405.\nDescribe how will Allah’s enemies be gathered to the Fire. We seek refuge with Allah.\nحَتَّىٰٓ إِذَا مَا جَآءُوهَا شَهِدَ عَلَيۡهِمۡ سَمۡعُهُمۡ وَأَبۡصَٰرُهُمۡ وَجُلُودُهُم بِمَا كَانُواْ يَعۡمَلُونَ ٢٠\nThese three faculties are singled out for mention because most sins are committed by means of them or because of them. Al-Saadi: 747.\nThese three faculties are singled out for mention. Why?\nwords\nفَقَضَاهُنَّOriginated, completed\nبِمَصَابِيحَShining stars\nصَاعِقَةًAn enormous punishment\nصَرصَرًاVery cold and roaring wind\nنَحِسَاتٍInauspicious\nالهُونِHumiliating\nيُوزَعُونَDriven [assembled] in rows"],[479,"§Fussilat\ndeeds\nIdentify those who make sins appealing to you and avoid their company.\nAsk Allah, persistently, to give you a righteous companion and keep bad ones away from you.\nListen to one of the good reciters of the Quran while reflecting on the verses.\nguid\nKeep good assumption about Allah, unlike the polytheists who have negative assumption of Him.\nSome people endure patiently for the sake of obeying Allah, while others are patient for the sake of disobeying Him.\nWhen the leaders' commands are contrary to Allah’s commands, they and those who follow them will perish.\nrefl\nوَمَا كُنتُمۡ تَسۡتَتِرُونَ أَن يَشۡهَدَ عَلَيۡكُمۡ سَمۡعُكُمۡ وَلَآ أَبۡصَٰرُكُمۡ وَلَا جُلُودُكُمۡ\nThis has two possible interpretations, first: You could not hide from your hearing, sight, and skins, because they are part of you, so you could not guard against that, hence they testified against you. Second: You did not guard against the testimony of your hearing, sight, and skins, because you did not care about their testimony, nor did you think that they would testify against you. Ibn Juzay: 2/291.\nWhat is meant by: (You were not hiding)? What lesson is learned from this verse?.\nوَذَٰلِكُمۡ ظَنُّكُمُ ٱلَّذِي ظَنَنتُم بِرَبِّكُمۡ أَرۡدَىٰكُمۡ فَأَصۡبَحۡتُم مِّنَ ٱلۡخَٰسِرِينَ ٢٣\nAlhasan Al-Basri said: \"Some people were diverted by false wishes until they passed away without doing a single good deed, and one of them used to say: I have good expectations of my Lord, but he was lying! If he had good expectations of Allah, he would have done good deeds.\" Al-Qurtubi: 18/409-410.\nExplain when having good expectations of Allah can be misplaced.\n۞وَقَيَّضۡنَا لَهُمۡ قُرَنَآءَ فَزَيَّنُواْ لَهُم مَّا بَيۡنَ أَيۡدِيهِمۡ وَمَا خَلۡفَهُمۡ\nMeaning: We set aside devils for them. Moreover, it is said: We sent associates from jinn, devils, and humans to make their sins appealing to them. Al-Qurtubi: 18/411.\nThis verse describes a sign of Allah's wrath upon the servant. What is it?\nوَقَالَ ٱلَّذِينَ كَفَرُواْ لَا تَسۡمَعُواْ لِهَٰذَا ٱلۡقُرۡءَانِ وَٱلۡغَوۡاْ فِيهِ لَعَلَّكُمۡ تَغۡلِبُونَ ٢٦\nThis is the work of those who call others to misguidance and falsehood in order to silence ones who speak the truth with evidence through intimidation and alluring. They do not let people exchange arguments because they surely know that their opponents’ argument is strong, thus, they try to hide and refute it by means of deceit and fabrication. When their plots fail and they see the rays of truth about to spread among people, who still have some goodness and prudence, they resort to ill speech by blowing into the trumpets of futility. Ibn Ashur: 24/277.\nGiven this verse, describe one of the traits of misguided people in warding off the truth.\nوَقَالَ ٱلَّذِينَ كَفَرُواْ لَا تَسۡمَعُواْ لِهَٰذَا ٱلۡقُرۡءَانِ وَٱلۡغَوۡاْ فِيهِ لَعَلَّكُمۡ تَغۡلِبُونَ ٢٦\nThis was testimony from the enemies, for the truth becomes clearer when its enemies testify in its favor. They thought that they could not defeat the one who brought it except by turning away and urging one another to do so, and what may be understood from their words is that if they did not do that, and instead they listened to it and paid attention to it, they would not be able to gain the upper hand. Al-Saadi: 748.\nThis verse presents a testimony by the disbelievers for the truth. How?\nوَقَالَ ٱلَّذِينَ كَفَرُواْ لَا تَسۡمَعُواْ لِهَٰذَا ٱلۡقُرۡءَانِ وَٱلۡغَوۡاْ فِيهِ لَعَلَّكُمۡ تَغۡلِبُونَ ٢٦\nIbn Abbas (k) said: \"It means: Speak noisily.\" Some of them used to enjoin others, saying: Whenever you see Muhammad reciting, oppose him by reading poems and engaging in ill speech. Mujahid said: Make noise by whistling and screeching. Ad-Dahhak said: Talk over his voice often so he may become confused. Al-Qurtubi: 4/65.\nThis verse describes some of corruptors' ways of preventing other from benefiting from the Quran and admonishments. Explain.\nوَقَالَ ٱلَّذِينَ كَفَرُواْ رَبَّنَآ أَرِنَا ٱلَّذَيۡنِ أَضَلَّانَا مِنَ ٱلۡجِنِّ وَٱلۡإِنسِ نَجۡعَلۡهُمَا تَحۡتَ أَقۡدَامِنَا لِيَكُونَا مِنَ ٱلۡأَسۡفَلِينَ ٢٩\nAllah mentions what will the disbelievers say on the Day of Resurrection when they enter the Fire and see the great terror in which they will be. They will begin thinking about who was behind their misguidance, their rage will become intensified and wish that those responsible receive the worst punishment, saying: (Our Lord, show us those who misled us). Ibn Atiyah: 5/14.\nWhat causes the inhabitants of the Fire to ask those who misled them from jinn and men to be under their feet?\nwords\nتَستَتِرُونَHiding when committing sins\nمَثوىًAbode\nيَستَعتِبُواThey ask to make amend, forgiveness\nفَمَا هُم مِنَ المُعتَبِينَThey will not be allowed to do so\nوَقَيَّضنَاWe assigned"]])